  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing WaveCanvas Component**\n\nI\'m currently focused on building the `WaveCanvas` component using React. This includes a full HTML5 2D canvas simulation of electromagnetic wavefronts, rays, E-fields, and evanescent decay. It will be smooth and evolve at 60fps using `requestAnimationFrame`, with the phase managed through `phaseRef` mutation.\n\n\n**Visualizing Wave Properties**\n\nI\'ve made progress on the rendering, focusing on the visual aspects. I\'m rendering the top and bottom halves with optical density shading. Wavefronts are now animated, with exact wavelength scaling and real amplitude weighting for incident, reflected, and refracted paths. I\'m also working on the evanescent wave display during TIR, showing its exponential decay. Rays with arrowheads are displayed as well.\n\n\n**Adding E-field Polarization**\n\nI\'m now incorporating E-field polarization vectors, including both TM and TE modes, to provide a more complete picture. I\'m focusing on clean, concise representations: oscillating arrows for TM and circle-dot/cross indicators for TE. I also plan on adding crisp normal lines and angle arcs.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Control Panel**\n\nI\'m now designing the interactive control panel with dropdowns, sliders, and toggle switches. I\'m focusing on providing instant exploration of phenomena. I\'m implementing a precision incident angle slider with numeric readout and quick jump actions. I\'ve added medium material dropdowns and sliders for refractive indices. I\'m working on the polarization toggle, and a spectrum band selector with a wavelength/frequency slider.\n\n**Implementing Regime Identifier Panel**\n\nI\'m making progress on the automatic wave propagation characteristic identifier panel. I\'m incorporating an active regime banner with a status glyph and semantic color. I\'m designing the summary explanation and defining three identified characteristics for the active regime. I\'m also preparing a six-cell precision metric grid for the display.\n\n\n**Calculating Fresnel Metrics**\n\nI\'m now calculating a suite of metrics to populate the Fresnel chart. This includes the refraction angle, effective reflection and transmission powers (with s and p components), characteristic angles, reflection phase shifts, and wavelength/phase velocity in the second medium.\n\n\n**Developing Inverse Identifier**\n\nI\'m now building the `InverseIdentifierView` tool, a fully interactive lab environment. It will let users identify wave propagation characteristics from measurements. I\'m implementing a mode-segmented selector for Snell\'s law, critical angle, and Brewster\'s angle. I\'ve included mystery measurement presets, and a button to source from the current simulation. The tool will have explicit numeric inputs with inline validation, formula derivation traces, an estimated electromagnetic properties grid, material fingerprint matching, and Fresnel diagnostic.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "M8kGa6iML6eA694Pg9XnaA"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_17340900066777250969"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import React, { useEffect, useRef, useState } from \'react\';\\nimport { Pause, Play, RotateCcw, StepForward } from \'lucide-react\';\\nimport {\\n  clamp,\\n  degToRad,\\n  formatWavelength,\\n  radToDeg,\\n  WavePhysicsResult,\\n  wavelengthToColor,\\n} from \'../physics/emPhysics\';\\nimport { PolarizationMode } from \'../physics/materials\';\\n\\nexport interface WaveLayerToggles {\\n  wavefronts: boolean;\\n  rays: boolean;\\n  eField: boolean;\\n  angles: boolean;\\n}\\n\\ninterface WaveCanvasProps {\\n  physics: WavePhysicsResult;\\n  polarization: PolarizationMode;\\n  wavelengthVacuumNm: number;\\n  material1Label: string;\\n  material2Label: string;\\n  onChangeIncidentAngle: (angleDeg: number) => void;\\n  onResetSimulation: () => void;\\n}\\n\\ninterface ProbeState {\\n  active: boolean;\\n  xPx: number;\\n  yPx: number;\\n  medium: 1 | 2;\\n  normX: number;\\n  normZ: number;\\n  angleFromNormalDeg: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport const WaveCanvas: React.FC<WaveCanvasProps> = ({\\n  physics,\\n  polarization,\\n  wavelengthVacuumNm,\\n  material1Label,\\n  material2Label,\\n  onChangeIncidentAngle,\\n  onResetSimulation,\\n}) => {\\n  const containerRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement | null>(null);\\n  const canvasRef = useRef<HTMLCanvasElement | null>(null);\\n\\n  const [isPlaying, setIsPlaying] = useState(true);\\n  const [speedMultiplier, setSpeedMultiplier] = useState(1.0);\\n  const [layers, setLayers] = useState<WaveLayerToggles>({\\n    wavefronts: true,\\n    rays: true,\\n    eField: true,\\n    angles: true,\\n  });\\n  const [isDraggingSource, setIsDraggingSource] = useState(false);\\n  const [probe, setProbe] = useState<ProbeState>({\\n    active: false,\\n    xPx: 0,\\n    yPx: 0,\\n    medium: 1,\\n    normX: 0,\\n    normZ: 0,\\n    angleFromNormalDeg: 0,\\n  });\\n\\n  // Mutable animation refs to avoid React re-renders at 60Hz\\n  const phaseRef = useRef(0);\\n  const isPlayingRef = useRef(isPlaying);\\n  const speedRef = useRef(speedMultiplier);\\n  const physicsRef = useRef(physics);\\n  const polarizationRef = useRef(polarization);\\n  const wavelengthRef = useRef(wavelengthVacuumNm);\\n  const layersRef = useRef(layers);\\n  const labelsRef = useRef({ m1: material1Label, m2: material2Label });\\n\\n  isPlayingRef.current = isPlaying;\\n  speedRef.current = speedMultiplier;\\n  physicsRef.current = physics;\\n  polarizationRef.current = polarization;\\n  wavelengthRef.current = wavelengthVacuumNm;\\n  layersRef.current = layers;\\n  labelsRef.current = { m1: material1Label, m2: material2Label };\\n\\n  const drawFrame = () => {\\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n    if (!canvas) return;\\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext(\'2d\');\\n    if (!ctx) return;\\n\\n    const dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);\\n    const width = canvas.width / dpr;\\n    const height = canvas.height / dpr;\\n    if (width <= 0 || height <= 0) return;\\n\\n    const p = physicsRef.current;\\n    const pol = polarizationRef.current;\\n    const ly = layersRef.current;\\n    const phase = phaseRef.current;\\n    const waveHex = wavelengthToColor(wavelengthRef.current);\\n\\n    ctx.save();\\n    ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);\\n\\n    const cx = width * 0.5;\\n    const cy = height * 0.5;\\n    const maxRayLen = Math.min(width * 0.46, height * 0.45);\\n\\n    // 1. Medium 1 (Top) & Medium 2 (Bottom) backgrounds shaded subtly by refractive index\\n    const m1Alpha = clamp((p.n1 - 1.0) * 0.085, 0, 0.24);\\n    const m2Alpha = clamp((p.n2 - 1.0) * 0.085, 0, 0.24);\\n\\n    ctx.fillStyle = \'#ffffff\';\\n    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, width, cy);\\n    ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(14, 165, 233, ${m1Alpha.toFixed(3)})`;\\n    ctx.fillRect(0, 0, width, cy);\\n\\n    ctx.fillStyle = \'#f8fafc\';\\n    ctx.fillRect(0, cy, width, height - cy);\\n    ctx.fillStyle = `rgba(37, 99, 235, ${(0.03 + m2Alpha).toFixed(3)})`;\\n    ctx.fillRect(0, cy, width, height - cy);\\n\\n    // Subtle scientific coordinate grid\\n    ctx.strokeStyle = \'rgba(148, 163, 184, 0.22)\';\\n    ctx.lineWidth = 1;\\n    const gridStep = 36;\\n    ctx.beginPath();\\n    for (let x = cx % gridStep; x < width; x += gridStep) {\\n      ctx.moveTo(x, 0);\\n      ctx.lineTo(x, height);\\n    }\\n    for (let y = cy % gridStep; y < height; y += gridStep) {\\n      ctx.moveTo(0, y);\\n      ctx.lineTo(width, y);\\n    }\\n    ctx.stroke();\\n\\n    // Base visual wavelength in pixels scaled cleanly by refractive index (lambda_m = lambda_0_px / n)\\n    const baseLambdaPx = 46;\\n    const lambda1Px = clamp(baseLambdaPx / p.n1, 14, 52);\\n    const lambda2Px = clamp(baseLambdaPx / p.n2, 12, 52);\\n\\n    const thetaI = p.incidentAngleRad;\\n    const sinI = Math.sin(thetaI);\\n    const cosI = Math.cos(thetaI);\\n\\n    // Unit propagation vectors (screen coordinates: +x right, +y down)\\n    // Incident travels from upper-left toward origin (cx, cy)\\n    const incDirX = sinI;\\n    const incDirY = cosI;\\n\\n    // Reflected travels from origin toward upper-right\\n    const refDirX = sinI;\\n    const refDirY = -cosI;\\n\\n    // Beam visual width\\n    const beamHalfWidth = Math.min(width, height) * 0.145;\\n\\n    // Helper: draw planar electromagnetic wavefronts along a finite beam corridor\\n    const drawWavefrontBeam = (\\n      originX: number,\\n      originY: number,\\n      dirX: number,\\n      dirY: number,\\n      length: number,\\n      lambdaPx: number,\\n      phaseOffsetRad: number,\\n      amplitudeWeight: number,\\n      strokeColor: string,\\n      clipRegion: \'top\' | \'bottom\',\\n      reverseTravel = false\\n    ) => {\\n      if (amplitudeWeight < 0.025) return;\\n\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      if (clipRegion === \'top\') {\\n        ctx.rect(0, 0, width, cy);\\n      } else {\\n        ctx.rect(0, cy, width, height - cy);\\n      }\\n      ctx.clip();\\n\\n      const perpX = -dirY;\\n      const perpY = dirX;\\n      const k = (2 * Math.PI) / lambdaPx;\\n\\n      // Subtle beam corridor guide\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.moveTo(originX + perpX * beamHalfWidth, originY + perpY * beamHalfWidth);\\n      ctx.lineTo(\\n        originX + dirX * length + perpX * beamHalfWidth,\\n        originY + dirY * length + perpY * beamHalfWidth\\n      );\\n      ctx.lineTo(\\n        originX + dirX * length - perpX * beamHalfWidth,\\n        originY + dirY * length - perpY * beamHalfWidth\\n      );\\n      ctx.lineTo(originX - perpX * beamHalfWidth, originY - perpY * beamHalfWidth);\\n      ctx.closePath();\\n      ctx.fillStyle = hexToRgba(strokeColor, 0.045 * amplitudeWeight);\\n      ctx.fill();\\n\\n      // Draw crisp sinusoidal wavefront crests & troughs\\n      const stepPx = 3;\\n      for (let s = 0; s <= length; s += stepPx) {\\n        const distFromOrigin = reverseTravel ? -s : s;\\n        const val = Math.cos(k * distFromOrigin - phase + phaseOffsetRad);\\n        if (Math.abs(val) < 0.25) continue;\\n\\n        const alpha = Math.pow(Math.abs(val), 1.6) * 0.55 * amplitudeWeight;\\n        const px = originX + dirX * s;\\n        const py = originY + dirY * s;\\n\\n        ctx.strokeStyle =\\n          val >= 0\\n            ? hexToRgba(strokeColor, alpha)\\n            : hexToRgba(\'#475569\', alpha * 0.42);\\n        ctx.lineWidth = val >= 0 ? 2.1 : 1.1;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.moveTo(px - perpX * beamHalfWidth, py - perpY * beamHalfWidth);\\n        ctx.lineTo(px + perpX * beamHalfWidth, py + perpY * beamHalfWidth);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n      }\\n      ctx.restore();\\n    };\\n\\n    // Helper: draw oscillating E-field polarization vectors along a ray\\n    const drawEFieldVectors = (\\n      startX: number,\\n      startY: number,\\n      dirX: number,\\n      dirY: number,\\n      length: number,\\n      lambdaPx: number,\\n      phaseOffsetRad: number,\\n      amplitudeWeight: number,\\n      color: string,\\n      clipRegion: \'top\' | \'bottom\',\\n      reverseTravel = false\\n    ) => {\\n      if (amplitudeWeight < 0.06) return;\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      if (clipRegion === \'top\') {\\n        ctx.rect(0, 0, width, cy);\\n      } else {\\n        ctx.rect(0, cy, width, height - cy);\\n      }\\n      ctx.clip();\\n\\n      const perpX = -dirY;\\n      const perpY = dirX;\\n      const k = (2 * Math.PI) / lambdaPx;\\n      const maxVecLen = 22 * amplitudeWeight;\\n\\n      if (pol === \'TM\' || pol === \'UNPOLARIZED\') {\\n        // Transverse in-plane E-field wave envelope + vector arrows\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = hexToRgba(color, 0.85 * amplitudeWeight);\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        for (let s = 8; s <= length - 8; s += 3) {\\n          const dist = reverseTravel ? -s : s;\\n          const eVal = Math.sin(k * dist - phase + phaseOffsetRad) * maxVecLen;\\n          const x = startX + dirX * s + perpX * eVal;\\n          const y = startY + dirY * s + perpY * eVal;\\n          if (s === 8) ctx.moveTo(x, y);\\n          else ctx.lineTo(x, y);\\n        }\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n\\n        // Discrete vector ticks perpendicular to ray\\n        const arrowSpacing = Math.max(12, lambdaPx * 0.35);\\n        for (let s = 14; s <= length - 14; s += arrowSpacing) {\\n          const dist = reverseTravel ? -s : s;\\n          const eVal = Math.sin(k * dist - phase + phaseOffsetRad) * maxVecLen;\\n          if (Math.abs(eVal) < 4) continue;\\n          const bx = startX + dirX * s;\\n          const by = startY + dirY * s;\\n          const tx = bx + perpX * eVal;\\n          const ty = by + perpY * eVal;\\n          ctx.beginPath();\\n          ctx.moveTo(bx, by);\\n          ctx.lineTo(tx, ty);\\n          ctx.strokeStyle = hexToRgba(color, 0.65 * amplitudeWeight);\\n          ctx.lineWidth = 1.25;\\n          ctx.stroke();\\n        }\\n      }\\n\\n      if (pol === \'TE\' || pol === \'UNPOLARIZED\') {\\n        // Out-of-plane E-field markers (dot = out of screen, cross = into screen)\\n        const spacing = Math.max(18, lambdaPx * 0.5);\\n        for (let s = 18; s <= length - 18; s += spacing) {\\n          const dist = reverseTravel ? -s : s;\\n          const eVal = Math.sin(k * dist - phase + phaseOffsetRad);\\n          const radius = 3.2 + Math.abs(eVal) * 4.5 * amplitudeWeight;\\n          const bx = startX + dirX * s;\\n          const by = startY + dirY * s;\\n\\n          ctx.fillStyle = \'#ffffff\';\\n          ctx.strokeStyle = hexToRgba(color, 0.85 * amplitudeWeight);\\n          ctx.lineWidth = 1.3;\\n          ctx.beginPath();\\n          ctx.arc(bx, by, radius, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n          ctx.fill();\\n          ctx.stroke();\\n\\n          if (eVal >= 0) {\\n            ctx.fillStyle = hexToRgba(color, 0.9 * amplitudeWeight);\\n            ctx.beginPath();\\n            ctx.arc(bx, by, 1.8, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n            ctx.fill();\\n          } else {\\n            const d = radius * 0.55;\\n            ctx.beginPath();\\n            ctx.moveTo(bx - d, by - d);\\n            ctx.lineTo(bx + d, by + d);\\n            ctx.moveTo(bx + d, by - d);\\n            ctx.lineTo(bx - d, by + d);\\n            ctx.stroke();\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n\\n      ctx.restore();\\n    };\\n\\n    // 2. Render Wavefronts (Incident, Reflected, Refracted or Evanescent)\\n    const refAmp = Math.sqrt(clamp(p.reflectanceEffective, 0, 1));\\n    const transAmp = Math.sqrt(clamp(p.transmittanceEffective, 0, 1));\\n    const refPhaseRad = degToRad(\\n      pol === \'TM\' ? p.phaseShiftPDeg : p.phaseShiftSDeg\\n    );\\n\\n    const beamLen = Math.hypot(width * 0.55, height * 0.55);\\n\\n    if (ly.wavefronts) {\\n      // Incident wavefronts traveling toward (cx, cy)\\n      drawWavefrontBeam(\\n        cx,\\n        cy,\\n        -incDirX,\\n        -incDirY,\\n        beamLen,\\n        lambda1Px,\\n        0,\\n        1.0,\\n        waveHex,\\n        \'top\',\\n        true\\n      );\\n\\n      // Reflected wavefronts traveling away from (cx, cy)\\n      drawWavefrontBeam(\\n        cx,\\n        cy,\\n        refDirX,\\n        refDirY,\\n        beamLen,\\n        lambda1Px,\\n        refPhaseRad,\\n        refAmp,\\n        \'#dc2626\',\\n        \'top\',\\n        false\\n      );\\n\\n      if (!p.isTotalInternalReflection && p.refractedAngleRad !== null) {\\n        const transDirX = Math.sin(p.refractedAngleRad);\\n        const transDirY = Math.cos(p.refractedAngleRad);\\n        drawWavefrontBeam(\\n          cx,\\n          cy,\\n          transDirX,\\n          transDirY,\\n          beamLen,\\n          lambda2Px,\\n          0,\\n          transAmp,\\n          \'#059669\',\\n          \'bottom\',\\n          false\\n        );\\n      } else if (p.isTotalInternalReflection) {\\n        // Evanescent wave decaying exponentially into Medium 2 and propagating along +x\\n        ctx.save();\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.rect(0, cy, width, height - cy);\\n        ctx.clip();\\n\\n        // Map real penetration depth ratio (delta_e / lambda_0) to crisp pixel decay depth\\n        const ratio =\\n          p.evanescentPenetrationDepthNm !== null\\n            ? clamp(p.evanescentPenetrationDepthNm / wavelengthRef.current, 0.08, 1.8)\\n            : 0.35;\\n        const decayDepthPx = clamp(ratio * 95, 18, height * 0.34);\\n        const kx = (2 * Math.PI * sinI) / lambda1Px;\\n\\n        const spanStart = cx - beamHalfWidth * 0.9;\\n        const spanEnd = Math.min(width - 12, cx + width * 0.42);\\n        const cols = 4;\\n\\n        for (let z = 2; z <= decayDepthPx * 2.6; z += 4) {\\n          const decay = Math.exp(-z / decayDepthPx);\\n          if (decay < 0.04) break;\\n          for (let x = spanStart; x <= spanEnd; x += cols) {\\n            const dx = x - cx;\\n            const envX =\\n              dx < 0\\n                ? Math.exp(-Math.pow(dx / (beamHalfWidth * 0.7), 2))\\n                : Math.exp(-dx / (width * 0.32));\\n            const val = Math.cos(kx * dx - phase) * decay * envX;\\n            if (Math.abs(val) < 0.06) continue;\\n            ctx.fillStyle =\\n              val >= 0\\n                ? hexToRgba(\'#d97706\', Math.abs(val) * 0.65)\\n                : hexToRgba(\'#0f172a\', Math.abs(val) * 0.25);\\n            ctx.fillRect(x, cy + z, cols, 3.2);\\n          }\\n        }\\n\\n        // Draw penetration depth 1/e indicator bracket\\n        const bracketX = Math.min(width - 96, cx + 110);\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = \'#b45309\';\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.4;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.moveTo(bracketX, cy + 2);\\n        ctx.lineTo(bracketX, cy + decayDepthPx);\\n        ctx.moveTo(bracketX - 5, cy + decayDepthPx);\\n        ctx.lineTo(bracketX + 5, cy + decayDepthPx);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n\\n        ctx.font = \'500 11px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\';\\n        ctx.fillStyle = \'#92400e\';\\n        const depthLabel =\\n          p.evanescentPenetrationDepthNm !== null\\n            ? `\316\264e = ${formatWavelength(p.evanescentPenetrationDepthNm)}`\\n            : \'S\303\263ng suy gi\341\272\243m\';\\n        ctx.fillText(depthLabel, bracketX + 8, cy + decayDepthPx * 0.5 + 4);\\n        ctx.restore();\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // 3. Interface Boundary Line & Normal Line\\n    ctx.strokeStyle = \'#334155\';\\n    ctx.lineWidth = 1.75;\\n    ctx.beginPath();\\n    ctx.moveTo(0, cy);\\n    ctx.lineTo(width, cy);\\n    ctx.stroke();\\n\\n    if (ly.angles) {\\n      // Normal line (dashed vertical through origin)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.strokeStyle = \'#64748b\';\\n      ctx.lineWidth = 1.2;\\n      ctx.setLineDash([5, 5]);\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.moveTo(cx, 16);\\n      ctx.lineTo(cx, height - 16);\\n      ctx.stroke();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      ctx.font = \'500 11px \\\"Plus Jakarta Sans\\\", sans-serif\';\\n      ctx.fillStyle = \'#64748b\';\\n      ctx.fillText(\'Ph\303\241p tuy\341\272\277n (N)\', cx + 7, 26);\\n\\n      // Optional critical angle reference line in upper-left quadrant\\n      if (p.criticalAngleDeg !== null) {\\n        const cRad = degToRad(p.criticalAngleDeg);\\n        const cLen = maxRayLen * 0.85;\\n        ctx.save();\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = \'rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.55)\';\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.1;\\n        ctx.setLineDash([3, 4]);\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.moveTo(cx, cy);\\n        ctx.lineTo(cx - Math.sin(cRad) * cLen, cy - Math.cos(cRad) * cLen);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n        ctx.restore();\\n\\n        ctx.font = \'500 10.5px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\';\\n        ctx.fillStyle = \'#b45309\';\\n        ctx.fillText(\\n          `\316\270c=${p.criticalAngleDeg.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n          cx - Math.sin(cRad) * (cLen * 0.72) - 46,\\n          cy - Math.cos(cRad) * (cLen * 0.72)\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // 4. E-field oscillation overlays along rays\\n    if (ly.eField) {\\n      drawEFieldVectors(\\n        cx,\\n        cy,\\n        -incDirX,\\n        -incDirY,\\n        maxRayLen * 0.92,\\n        lambda1Px,\\n        0,\\n        1.0,\\n        waveHex,\\n        \'top\',\\n        true\\n      );\\n      if (refAmp > 0.08) {\\n        drawEFieldVectors(\\n          cx,\\n          cy,\\n          refDirX,\\n          refDirY,\\n          maxRayLen * 0.92,\\n          lambda1Px,\\n          refPhaseRad,\\n          refAmp,\\n          \'#dc2626\',\\n          \'top\',\\n          false\\n        );\\n      }\\n      if (!p.isTotalInternalReflection && p.refractedAngleRad !== null && transAmp > 0.08) {\\n        drawEFieldVectors(\\n          cx,\\n          cy,\\n          Math.sin(p.refractedAngleRad),\\n          Math.cos(p.refractedAngleRad),\\n          maxRayLen * 0.92,\\n          lambda2Px,\\n          0,\\n          transAmp,\\n          \'#059669\',\\n          \'bottom\',\\n          false\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // 5. Crisp Ray Arrows (Incident, Reflected, Refracted)\\n    const srcX = cx - incDirX * maxRayLen;\\n    const srcY = cy - incDirY * maxRayLen;\\n\\n    if (ly.rays) {\\n      // Incident ray\\n      drawRayArrow(ctx, srcX, srcY, cx, cy, waveHex, 2.8, 1.0);\\n\\n      // Reflected ray (opacity + thickness scales with sqrt(R))\\n      const refAlpha = clamp(0.18 + refAmp * 0.82, 0.18, 1);\\n      const refWidth = 1.4 + refAmp * 1.8;\\n      drawRayArrow(\\n        ctx,\\n        cx,\\n        cy,\\n        cx + refDirX * maxRayLen,\\n        cy + refDirY * maxRayLen,\\n        \'#dc2626\',\\n        refWidth,\\n        refAlpha\\n      );\\n\\n      // Refracted ray\\n      if (!p.isTotalInternalReflection && p.refractedAngleRad !== null) {\\n        const transAlpha = clamp(0.2 + transAmp * 0.8, 0.2, 1);\\n        const transWidth = 1.4 + transAmp * 1.8;\\n        drawRayArrow(\\n          ctx,\\n          cx,\\n          cy,\\n          cx + Math.sin(p.refractedAngleRad) * maxRayLen,\\n          cy + Math.cos(p.refractedAngleRad) * maxRayLen,\\n          \'#059669\',\\n          transWidth,\\n          transAlpha\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // 6. Angle Arcs & Numeric Annotations\\n    if (ly.angles) {\\n      const arcR = 52;\\n      // Incident angle arc (measured from top normal -pi/2 counter-clockwise to incident ray)\\n      if (p.incidentAngleDeg > 1.5) {\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = waveHex;\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.arc(cx, cy, arcR, -Math.PI / 2 - thetaI, -Math.PI / 2);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n\\n        const midI = -Math.PI / 2 - thetaI * 0.5;\\n        ctx.font = \'600 11.5px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\';\\n        ctx.fillStyle = \'#0f172a\';\\n        ctx.fillText(\\n          `\316\270i ${p.incidentAngleDeg.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n          cx + Math.cos(midI) * (arcR + 14) - 24,\\n          cy + Math.sin(midI) * (arcR + 14)\\n        );\\n      }\\n\\n      // Reflected angle arc\\n      if (p.incidentAngleDeg > 1.5 && p.reflectanceEffective > 0.002) {\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = \'#dc2626\';\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.4;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.arc(cx, cy, arcR - 10, -Math.PI / 2, -Math.PI / 2 + thetaI);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n\\n        const midR = -Math.PI / 2 + thetaI * 0.5;\\n        ctx.font = \'500 11px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\';\\n        ctx.fillStyle = \'#b91c1c\';\\n        ctx.fillText(\\n          `\316\270r ${p.reflectedAngleDeg.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n          cx + Math.cos(midR) * (arcR + 8) + 2,\\n          cy + Math.sin(midR) * (arcR + 8)\\n        );\\n      }\\n\\n      // Refracted angle arc\\n      if (!p.isTotalInternalReflection && p.refractedAngleRad !== null && p.refractedAngleDeg! > 1.5) {\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = \'#059669\';\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.arc(cx, cy, arcR, Math.PI / 2 - p.refractedAngleRad, Math.PI / 2);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n\\n        const midT = Math.PI / 2 - p.refractedAngleRad * 0.5;\\n        ctx.font = \'600 11.5px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\';\\n        ctx.fillStyle = \'#047857\';\\n        ctx.fillText(\\n          `\316\270t ${p.refractedAngleDeg!.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n          cx + Math.cos(midT) * (arcR + 16) + 2,\\n          cy + Math.sin(midT) * (arcR + 16) + 4\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // 7. Interactive Emitter Handle on Incident Ray\\n    ctx.save();\\n    ctx.beginPath();\\n    ctx.arc(srcX, srcY, 10, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n    ctx.fillStyle = \'#ffffff\';\\n    ctx.fill();\\n    ctx.lineWidth = 2.5;\\n    ctx.strokeStyle = waveHex;\\n    ctx.stroke();\\n\\n    ctx.beginPath();\\n    ctx.arc(srcX, srcY, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n    ctx.fillStyle = waveHex;\\n    ctx.fill();\\n    ctx.restore();\\n\\n    // Origin incidence marker\\n    ctx.beginPath();\\n    ctx.arc(cx, cy, 4, 0, Math.PI * 2);\\n    ctx.fillStyle = \'#0f172a\';\\n    ctx.fill();\\n\\n    // 8. Medium Labels (Corner HUD inside canvas, crisp typography, no pill boxes)\\n    ctx.font = \'600 12px \\\"Plus Jakarta Sans\\\", sans-serif\';\\n    ctx.fillStyle = \'#0f172a\';\\n    ctx.fillText(`M\303\264i tr\306\260\341\273\235ng 1: ${labelsRef.current.m1}`, 16, 26);\\n    ctx.font = \'500 11px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\';\\n    ctx.fillStyle = \'#475569\';\\n    ctx.fillText(\\n      `n\342\202\201 = ${p.n1.toFixed(3)} \302\267 \316\265r\342\202\201 = ${p.permittivity1.toFixed(2)} \302\267 Z\342\202\201 = ${p.impedance1Ohm.toFixed(1)} \316\251`,\\n      16,\\n      44\\n    );\\n\\n    ctx.font = \'600 12px \\\"Plus Jakarta Sans\\\", sans-serif\';\\n    ctx.fillStyle = \'#0f172a\';\\n    ctx.fillText(`M\303\264i tr\306\260\341\273\235ng 2: ${labelsRef.current.m2}`, 16, cy + 26);\\n    ctx.font = \'500 11px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\';\\n    ctx.fillStyle = \'#475569\';\\n    ctx.fillText(\\n      `n\342\202\202 = ${p.n2.toFixed(3)} \302\267 \316\265r\342\202\202 = ${p.permittivity2.toFixed(2)} \302\267 Z\342\202\202 = ${p.impedance2Ohm.toFixed(1)} \316\251`,\\n      16,\\n      cy + 44\\n    );\\n\\n    // Subtle right-hand energy flux readout\\n    ctx.textAlign = \'right\';\\n    ctx.font = \'500 11px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\';\\n    ctx.fillStyle = \'#b91c1c\';\\n    ctx.fillText(`Ph\341\272\243n x\341\272\241 R = ${(p.reflectanceEffective * 100).toFixed(1)}%`, width - 16, 26);\\n    ctx.fillStyle = p.isTotalInternalReflection ? \'#b45309\' : \'#047857\';\\n    ctx.fillText(\\n      p.isTotalInternalReflection\\n        ? \'Truy\341\273\201n xa T = 0.0% (S\303\263ng suy gi\341\272\243m)\'\\n        : `Truy\341\273\201n qua T = ${(p.transmittanceEffective * 100).toFixed(1)}%`,\\n      width - 16,\\n      cy + 26\\n    );\\n    ctx.textAlign = \'left\';\\n\\n    ctx.restore();\\n  };\\n\\n  // Resize observer + animation loop mounted once\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n    const container = containerRef.current;\\n    if (!canvas || !container) return;\\n\\n    const resizeCanvas = () => {\\n      const rect = container.getBoundingClientRect();\\n      const dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);\\n      canvas.width = Math.max(300, Math.floor(rect.width * dpr));\\n      canvas.height = Math.max(340, Math.floor(rect.height * dpr));\\n      drawFrame();\\n    };\\n\\n    resizeCanvas();\\n    const observer = new ResizeObserver(resizeCanvas);\\n    observer.observe(container);\\n\\n    const prefersReducedMotion =\\n      typeof window !== \'undefined\' &&\\n      window.matchMedia &&\\n      window.matchMedia(\'(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)\').matches;\\n\\n    let rafId = 0;\\n    let lastTs = performance.now();\\n\\n    const tick = (now: number) => {\\n      const dt = Math.min(0.05, (now - lastTs) / 1000);\\n      lastTs = now;\\n      if (isPlayingRef.current && !prefersReducedMotion) {\\n        phaseRef.current = (phaseRef.current + dt * 4.2 * speedRef.current) % (Math.PI * 200);\\n      }\\n      drawFrame();\\n      rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\\n    };\\n\\n    rafId = requestAnimationFrame(tick);\\n\\n    return () => {\\n      cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);\\n      observer.disconnect();\\n    };\\n  }, []);\\n\\n  // Re-draw immediately on prop changes when paused\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    drawFrame();\\n  }, [physics, polarization, wavelengthVacuumNm, material1Label, material2Label, layers]);\\n\\n  const updateAngleFromPointer = (clientX: number, clientY: number) => {\\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n    if (!canvas) return;\\n    const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\\n    const x = clientX - rect.left;\\n    const y = clientY - rect.top;\\n    const cx = rect.width * 0.5;\\n    const cy = rect.height * 0.5;\\n\\n    const dx = cx - x; // positive to the left of normal\\n    const dy = cy - y; // positive above interface\\n    if (dy < 2) {\\n      onChangeIncidentAngle(89.0);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const clampedDx = Math.max(0, dx);\\n    const angle = radToDeg(Math.atan2(clampedDx, dy));\\n    onChangeIncidentAngle(Math.round(clamp(angle, 0, 89.5) * 10) / 10);\\n  };\\n\\n  const handlePointerDown = (e: React.PointerEvent<HTMLCanvasElement>) => {\\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n    if (!canvas) return;\\n    const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\\n    const y = e.clientY - rect.top;\\n    // Allow dragging anywhere in Medium 1 to aim the incident wave\\n    if (y <= rect.height * 0.52) {\\n      setIsDraggingSource(true);\\n      e.currentTarget.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);\\n      updateAngleFromPointer(e.clientX, e.clientY);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handlePointerMove = (e: React.PointerEvent<HTMLCanvasElement>) => {\\n    const canvas = canvasRef.current;\\n    if (!canvas) return;\\n    const rect = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\\n    const x = e.clientX - rect.left;\\n    const y = e.clientY - rect.top;\\n    const cx = rect.width * 0.5;\\n    const cy = rect.height * 0.5;\\n\\n    const normX = (x - cx) / (rect.width * 0.5);\\n    const normZ = (y - cy) / (rect.height * 0.5);\\n    const angleFromNormalDeg = radToDeg(Math.atan2(Math.abs(x - cx), Math.max(1, Math.abs(y - cy))));\\n\\n    setProbe({\\n      active: true,\\n      xPx: x,\\n      yPx: y,\\n      medium: y <= cy ? 1 : 2,\\n      normX,\\n      normZ,\\n      angleFromNormalDeg,\\n    });\\n\\n    if (isDraggingSource) {\\n      updateAngleFromPointer(e.clientX, e.clientY);\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handlePointerUp = (e: React.PointerEvent<HTMLCanvasElement>) => {\\n    if (isDraggingSource) {\\n      setIsDraggingSource(false);\\n      if (e.currentTarget.hasPointerCapture(e.pointerId)) {\\n        e.currentTarget.releasePointerCapture(e.pointerId);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  };\\n\\n  const handleStepFrame = () => {\\n    setIsPlaying(false);\\n    phaseRef.current += Math.PI / 4;\\n    drawFrame();\\n  };\\n\\n  const toggleLayer = (key: keyof WaveLayerToggles) => {\\n    setLayers((prev) => ({ ...prev, [key]: !prev[key] }));\\n  };\\n\\n  return (\\n    <section\\n      aria-label=\\\"S\303\242n kh\341\272\245u m\303\264 ph\341\273\217ng truy\341\273\201n s\303\263ng \304\221i\341\273\207n t\341\273\253\\\"\\n      className=\\\"bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl overflow-hidden\\\"\\n    >\\n      {/* Compact Instrument Toolbar */}\\n      <div className=\\\"flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70\\\">\\n        <div className=\\\"flex items-center gap-2\\\">\\n          <button\\n            type=\\\"button\\\"\\n            onClick={() => setIsPlaying((v) => !v)}\\n            className=\\\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium rounded-md bg-white border border-slate-200 text-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-100 transition-colors whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 cursor-pointer\\\"\\n          >\\n            {isPlaying ? <Pause className=\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5\\\" /> : <Play className=\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5\\\" />}\\n            {isPlaying ? \'T\341\272\241m d\341\273\253ng\' : \'Ph\303\241t s\303\263ng\'}\\n          </button>\\n\\n          <button\\n            type=\\\"button\\\"\\n            onClick={handleStepFrame}\\n            aria-label=\\\"B\306\260\341\273\233c khung s\303\263ng k\341\272\277 ti\341\272\277p\\\"\\n            className=\\\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium rounded-md bg-white border border-slate-200 text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 transition-colors whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 cursor-pointer\\\"\\n          >\\n            <StepForward className=\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5\\\" />\\n            B\306\260\341\273\233c pha\\n          </button>\\n\\n          <button\\n            type=\\\"button\\\"\\n            onClick={onResetSimulation}\\n            aria-label=\\\"\304\220\341\272\267t l\341\272\241i tham s\341\273\221 m\303\264 ph\341\273\217ng\\\"\\n            className=\\\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium rounded-md bg-white border border-slate-200 text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 transition-colors whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 cursor-pointer\\\"\\n          >\\n            <RotateCcw className=\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5\\\" />\\n            \304\220\341\272\267t l\341\272\241i\\n          </button>\\n\\n          <div className=\\\"hidden sm:flex items-center gap-1.5 pl-2 border-l border-slate-200 text-xs text-slate-600\\\">\\n            <label htmlFor=\\\"wave-speed-select\\\" className=\\\"whitespace-nowrap\\\">\\n              T\341\273\221c \304\221\341\273\231:\\n            </label>\\n            <select\\n              id=\\\"wave-speed-select\\\"\\n              value={speedMultiplier}\\n              onChange={(e) => setSpeedMultiplier(Number(e.target.value))}\\n              className=\\\"bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded px-1.5 py-1 text-xs font-mono text-slate-800\\\"\\n            >\\n              <option value={0.5}>0.5\303\227</option>\\n              <option value={1}>1.0\303\227</option>\\n              <option value={1.8}>1.8\303\227</option>\\n            </select>\\n          </div>\\n        </div>\\n\\n        {/* Layer Visibility Toggles */}\\n        <div\\n          role=\\\"group\\\"\\n          aria-label=\\\"L\341\273\233p hi\341\273\203n th\341\273\213 m\303\264 ph\341\273\217ng\\\"\\n          className=\\\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1 bg-slate-100 p-1 rounded-lg\\\"\\n        >\\n          {(\\n            [\\n              [\'wavefronts\', \'S\303\263ng ph\341\272\263ng\'],\\n              [\'rays\', \'Tia s\303\263ng\'],\\n              [\'eField\', \'Tr\306\260\341\273\235ng E\'],\\n              [\'angles\', \'G\303\263c & Ph\303\241p tuy\341\272\277n\'],\\n            ] as const\\n          ).map(([key, label]) => (\\n            <button\\n              key={key}\\n              type=\\\"button\\\"\\n              aria-pressed={layers[key]}\\n              onClick={() => toggleLayer(key)}\\n              className={`px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium rounded-md transition-colors whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 cursor-pointer ${\\n                layers[key]\\n                  ? \'bg-white text-slate-900 shadow-xs\'\\n                  : \'text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-900\'\\n              }`}\\n            >\\n              {label}\\n            </button>\\n          ))}\\n        </div>\\n      </div>\\n\\n      {/* Main Canvas Stage */}\\n      <div\\n        ref={containerRef}\\n        className=\\\"relative w-full h-[380px] sm:h-[430px] select-none bg-white\\\"\\n        data-testid=\\\"em-wave-canvas-container\\\"\\n        data-regime={physics.classification.code}\\n      >\\n        <canvas\\n          ref={canvasRef}\\n          data-testid=\\\"em-wave-canvas\\\"\\n          onPointerDown={handlePointerDown}\\n          onPointerMove={handlePointerMove}\\n          onPointerUp={handlePointerUp}\\n          onPointerLeave={() => {\\n            setProbe((prev) => ({ ...prev, active: false }));\\n          }}\\n          className={`w-full h-full block ${\\n            isDraggingSource ? \'cursor-grabbing\' : \'cursor-crosshair\'\\n          }`}\\n          aria-label=\\\"Bi\341\273\203u \304\221\341\273\223 tr\341\273\261c quan kh\303\272c x\341\272\241 v\303\240 ph\341\272\243n x\341\272\241 s\303\263ng \304\221i\341\273\207n t\341\273\253 qua m\341\272\267t ph\303\242n c\303\241ch hai m\303\264i tr\306\260\341\273\235ng\\\"\\n        />\\n\\n        {/* Subtle Bottom Coordinate Probe & Interaction Hint */}\\n        <div className=\\\"pointer-events-none absolute bottom-2.5 left-4 right-4 flex items-center justify-between text-[11px] font-mono text-slate-500\\\">\\n          <span>K\303\251o ngu\341\273\223n ph\303\241t \341\273\237 m\303\264i tr\306\260\341\273\235ng 1 \304\221\341\273\203 thay \304\221\341\273\225i g\303\263c t\341\273\233i \316\270i tr\341\273\261c ti\341\272\277p</span>\\n          {probe.active && (\\n            <span className=\\\"hidden sm:inline bg-white/90 px-2 py-0.5 rounded border border-slate-200 tabular-nums text-slate-700\\\">\\n              M\303\264i tr\306\260\341\273\235ng {probe.medium} \302\267 x={probe.normX.toFixed(2)} \302\267 z={probe.normZ.toFixed(2)} \302\267 \342\210\240N=\\n              {probe.angleFromNormalDeg.toFixed(1)}\302\260\\n            </span>\\n          )}\\n        </div>\\n      </div>\\n    </section>\\n  );\\n};\\n\\nfunction drawRayArrow(\\n  ctx: CanvasRenderingContext2D,\\n  x1: number,\\n  y1: number,\\n  x2: number,\\n  y2: number,\\n  color: string,\\n  lineWidth: number,\\n  alpha: number\\n) {\\n  ctx.save();\\n  ctx.strokeStyle = hexToRgba(color, alpha);\\n  ctx.fillStyle = hexToRgba(color, alpha);\\n  ctx.lineWidth = lineWidth;\\n  ctx.lineCap = \'round\';\\n\\n  ctx.beginPath();\\n  ctx.moveTo(x1, y1);\\n  ctx.lineTo(x2, y2);\\n  ctx.stroke();\\n\\n  // Midpoint directional arrow\\n  const mx = x1 + (x2 - x1) * 0.56;\\n  const my = y1 + (y2 - y1) * 0.56;\\n  const angle = Math.atan2(y2 - y1, x2 - x1);\\n  const headLen = 9;\\n\\n  ctx.beginPath();\\n  ctx.moveTo(mx, my);\\n  ctx.lineTo(\\n    mx - headLen * Math.cos(angle - Math.PI / 6),\\n    my - headLen * Math.sin(angle - Math.PI / 6)\\n  );\\n  ctx.lineTo(\\n    mx - headLen * Math.cos(angle + Math.PI / 6),\\n    my - headLen * Math.sin(angle + Math.PI / 6)\\n  );\\n  ctx.closePath();\\n  ctx.fill();\\n  ctx.restore();\\n}\\n\\nfunction hexToRgba(hex: string, alpha: number): string {\\n  const clean = hex.replace(\'#\', \'\');\\n  const full =\\n    clean.length === 3\\n      ? clean\\n          .split(\'\')\\n          .map((c) => c + c)\\n          .join(\'\')\\n      : clean;\\n  const num = parseInt(full, 16);\\n  const r = (num >> 16) & 255;\\n  const g = (num >> 8) & 255;\\n  const b = num & 255;\\n  return `rgba(${r}, ${g}, ${b}, ${clamp(alpha, 0, 1).toFixed(3)})`;\\n}\\n\",\"Description\":\"Create interactive 2D Canvas electromagnetic wavefront, ray, E-field, and evanescent wave simulator\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/WaveCanvas.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Creating WaveCanvas simulation component\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create WaveCanvas component\"}"
