  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Defects**\n\nI\'m incredibly impressed by the sharpness and authenticity of these captures. The real visual defects are instantly apparent when viewing the rendered screenshots and video. Ultra Mode visual critique has proven to be essential. It is so much easier to understand these issues in a visual format.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Mobile Defects**\n\nI\'ve isolated a critical defect: mobile navigation and reading order are major pain points. The top bar navigation is clipped, obscuring key functions. The control deck overlaps the simulation on initial paint. I propose a compact mobile navbar or a tab strip, or a similar 3-zone desktop design. I\'m focusing on user experience, and this has to be the top priority.\n\n\n**Optimizing Mobile Layout**\n\nI\'m zeroing in on mobile layout, aiming for a clean, non-clipped presentation. The current thought is to use a compact, second-row tab bar within `<main>` on screens smaller than medium, while keeping the `<header>` single-row and mobile sticky. I\'m also considering putting the mobile nav bar inside `<main>` for maximum visibility and tap-ability on 390px screens. To enhance the mobile user experience, I\'m thinking of reordering the simulator grid by swapping the order of the main stage and control deck.\n\n**Refining Overlap Analysis**\n\nI\'ve been examining the overlap of labels and visual elements in desktop screenshots. Specifically, the angle labels `\316\270t 27.8\302\260` and `\316\270i 45.0\302\260` in `r1-desktop.png` are slightly obscuring visual elements, and I am evaluating how to address this.\n\n\n**Improving Visual Clarity**\n\nI\'m focused on improving the visual clarity in the TIR renders, particularly `r1-tir.png`. The critical angle label (`\316\270c=41.3\302\260`) is currently overlapping the red incident ray, and the reflected angle label is also colliding. My plan is to add a subtle white halo to all angle annotations and reposition them outside the arc radius along their bisectors to avoid collisions. I\'ll also boost the contrast of the evanescent wave to make its characteristics more obvious.\n\n\n**Addressing Text Truncation**\n\nI\'ve homed in on specific text truncation in the desktop view, pinpointing the problematic quick preset buttons in `ControlDeck.tsx`. My concrete action is to ensure concise Vietnamese labels (\"G\303\263c Brewster\" and \"Ph\341\272\243n x\341\272\241 to\303\240n ph\341\272\247n\") that will never be truncated. I\'m also examining metric sub-label line wrapping and unit spacing, which is leading to awkward breaks in text within the `CharacteristicsPanel.tsx` component. I\'m aiming for single-line sub-labels and uniform baselines across the metric cells.\n\n**Improving Fresnel Chart Display**\n\nI\'m now checking the Fresnel chart visibility, both above the fold and in the log view.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "B8wGa5nJF5eD694P1-nR4Qk"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_4559453127707005676"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Add crisp haloed angle labels, clean label placement without ray collision, and clearer evanescent wave rendering in WaveCanvas.tsx\",\"EndLine\":495,\"Instruction\":\"Improve evanescent wave visibility and add clean white text halos and non-overlapping label positions for \316\270c, \316\270i, \316\270r, \316\270t, and \316\264e\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"        // Map real penetration depth ratio (delta_e / lambda_0) to crisp pixel decay depth\\n        const ratio =\\n          p.evanescentPenetrationDepthNm !== null\\n            ? clamp(p.evanescentPenetrationDepthNm / wavelengthRef.current, 0.1, 1.8)\\n            : 0.35;\\n        const decayDepthPx = clamp(ratio * 110, 26, height * 0.34);\\n        const kx = (2 * Math.PI * sinI) / lambda1Px;\\n\\n        const spanStart = cx - beamHalfWidth * 0.95;\\n        const spanEnd = Math.min(width - 12, cx + width * 0.44);\\n        const cols = 4;\\n\\n        for (let z = 2; z <= decayDepthPx * 2.8; z += 4) {\\n          const decay = Math.exp(-z / decayDepthPx);\\n          if (decay < 0.04) break;\\n          for (let x = spanStart; x <= spanEnd; x += cols) {\\n            const dx = x - cx;\\n            const envX =\\n              dx < 0\\n                ? Math.exp(-Math.pow(dx / (beamHalfWidth * 0.72), 2))\\n                : Math.exp(-dx / (width * 0.34));\\n            const val = Math.cos(kx * dx - phase) * decay * envX;\\n            if (Math.abs(val) < 0.05) continue;\\n            ctx.fillStyle =\\n              val >= 0\\n                ? hexToRgba(\'#d97706\', Math.abs(val) * 0.82)\\n                : hexToRgba(\'#0f172a\', Math.abs(val) * 0.32);\\n            ctx.fillRect(x, cy + z, cols, 3.4);\\n          }\\n        }\\n\\n        // Dashed 1/e decay horizon line\\n        ctx.save();\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = \'rgba(180, 83, 9, 0.45)\';\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1;\\n        ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.moveTo(cx - 20, cy + decayDepthPx);\\n        ctx.lineTo(Math.min(width - 120, cx + 150), cy + decayDepthPx);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n        ctx.restore();\\n\\n        // Draw penetration depth 1/e indicator bracket\\n        const bracketX = Math.min(width - 130, cx + 118);\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = \'#b45309\';\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.moveTo(bracketX, cy + 2);\\n        ctx.lineTo(bracketX, cy + decayDepthPx);\\n        ctx.moveTo(bracketX - 5, cy + decayDepthPx);\\n        ctx.lineTo(bracketX + 5, cy + decayDepthPx);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n\\n        const depthLabel =\\n          p.evanescentPenetrationDepthNm !== null\\n            ? `\316\264e = ${formatWavelength(p.evanescentPenetrationDepthNm)}`\\n            : \'S\303\263ng suy gi\341\272\243m\';\\n        drawHaloText(\\n          ctx,\\n          depthLabel,\\n          bracketX + 9,\\n          cy + Math.max(14, decayDepthPx * 0.55 + 3),\\n          \'#92400e\',\\n          \'600 11px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\',\\n          \'left\'\\n        );\\n        ctx.restore();\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // 3. Interface Boundary Line & Normal Line\\n    ctx.strokeStyle = \'#334155\';\\n    ctx.lineWidth = 1.75;\\n    ctx.beginPath();\\n    ctx.moveTo(0, cy);\\n    ctx.lineTo(width, cy);\\n    ctx.stroke();\\n\\n    if (ly.angles) {\\n      // Normal line (dashed vertical through origin)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.strokeStyle = \'#64748b\';\\n      ctx.lineWidth = 1.2;\\n      ctx.setLineDash([5, 5]);\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.moveTo(cx, 16);\\n      ctx.lineTo(cx, height - 16);\\n      ctx.stroke();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      drawHaloText(\\n        ctx,\\n        \'Ph\303\241p tuy\341\272\277n (N)\',\\n        cx + 8,\\n        24,\\n        \'#64748b\',\\n        \'500 11px \\\"Plus Jakarta Sans\\\", sans-serif\',\\n        \'left\'\\n      );\\n\\n      // Optional critical angle reference line in upper-left quadrant\\n      if (p.criticalAngleDeg !== null) {\\n        const cRad = degToRad(p.criticalAngleDeg);\\n        const cLen = maxRayLen * 0.96;\\n        ctx.save();\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = \'rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.65)\';\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.25;\\n        ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.moveTo(cx, cy);\\n        ctx.lineTo(cx - Math.sin(cRad) * cLen, cy - Math.cos(cRad) * cLen);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n        ctx.restore();\\n\\n        drawHaloText(\\n          ctx,\\n          `\316\270c = ${p.criticalAngleDeg.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n          cx - Math.sin(cRad) * (cLen * 0.88) - 8,\\n          cy - Math.cos(cRad) * (cLen * 0.88) - 6,\\n          \'#b45309\',\\n          \'600 11px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\',\\n          \'right\'\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // 4. E-field oscillation overlays along rays\\n    if (ly.eField) {\\n      drawEFieldVectors(\\n        cx,\\n        cy,\\n        -incDirX,\\n        -incDirY,\\n        maxRayLen * 0.92,\\n        lambda1Px,\\n        0,\\n        1.0,\\n        waveHex,\\n        \'top\',\\n        true\\n      );\\n      if (refAmp > 0.08) {\\n        drawEFieldVectors(\\n          cx,\\n          cy,\\n          refDirX,\\n          refDirY,\\n          maxRayLen * 0.92,\\n          lambda1Px,\\n          refPhaseRad,\\n          refAmp,\\n          \'#dc2626\',\\n          \'top\',\\n          false\\n        );\\n      }\\n      if (!p.isTotalInternalReflection && p.refractedAngleRad !== null && transAmp > 0.08) {\\n        drawEFieldVectors(\\n          cx,\\n          cy,\\n          Math.sin(p.refractedAngleRad),\\n          Math.cos(p.refractedAngleRad),\\n          maxRayLen * 0.92,\\n          lambda2Px,\\n          0,\\n          transAmp,\\n          \'#059669\',\\n          \'bottom\',\\n          false\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // 5. Crisp Ray Arrows (Incident, Reflected, Refracted)\\n    const srcX = cx - incDirX * maxRayLen;\\n    const srcY = cy - incDirY * maxRayLen;\\n\\n    if (ly.rays) {\\n      // Incident ray\\n      drawRayArrow(ctx, srcX, srcY, cx, cy, waveHex, 2.8, 1.0);\\n\\n      // Reflected ray (opacity + thickness scales with sqrt(R))\\n      const refAlpha = clamp(0.18 + refAmp * 0.82, 0.18, 1);\\n      const refWidth = 1.4 + refAmp * 1.8;\\n      drawRayArrow(\\n        ctx,\\n        cx,\\n        cy,\\n        cx + refDirX * maxRayLen,\\n        cy + refDirY * maxRayLen,\\n        \'#dc2626\',\\n        refWidth,\\n        refAlpha\\n      );\\n\\n      // Refracted ray\\n      if (!p.isTotalInternalReflection && p.refractedAngleRad !== null) {\\n        const transAlpha = clamp(0.2 + transAmp * 0.8, 0.2, 1);\\n        const transWidth = 1.4 + transAmp * 1.8;\\n        drawRayArrow(\\n          ctx,\\n          cx,\\n          cy,\\n          cx + Math.sin(p.refractedAngleRad) * maxRayLen,\\n          cy + Math.cos(p.refractedAngleRad) * maxRayLen,\\n          \'#059669\',\\n          transWidth,\\n          transAlpha\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // 6. Angle Arcs & Haloed Numeric Annotations (positioned cleanly along arc bisectors)\\n    if (ly.angles) {\\n      const arcR = 54;\\n      // Incident angle arc\\n      if (p.incidentAngleDeg > 1.5) {\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = waveHex;\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.8;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.arc(cx, cy, arcR, -Math.PI / 2 - thetaI, -Math.PI / 2);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n\\n        const midI = -Math.PI / 2 - thetaI * 0.45;\\n        const labelR = arcR + 22;\\n        drawHaloText(\\n          ctx,\\n          `\316\270i ${p.incidentAngleDeg.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n          cx + Math.cos(midI) * labelR - 6,\\n          cy + Math.sin(midI) * labelR,\\n          \'#0f172a\',\\n          \'600 11.5px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\',\\n          \'right\'\\n        );\\n      }\\n\\n      // Reflected angle arc\\n      if (p.incidentAngleDeg > 1.5 && p.reflectanceEffective > 0.002) {\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = \'#dc2626\';\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.arc(cx, cy, arcR - 12, -Math.PI / 2, -Math.PI / 2 + thetaI);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n\\n        const midR = -Math.PI / 2 + thetaI * 0.45;\\n        const labelR = arcR + 18;\\n        drawHaloText(\\n          ctx,\\n          `\316\270r ${p.reflectedAngleDeg.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n          cx + Math.cos(midR) * labelR + 6,\\n          cy + Math.sin(midR) * labelR,\\n          \'#b91c1c\',\\n          \'600 11px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\',\\n          \'left\'\\n        );\\n      }\\n\\n      // Refracted angle arc\\n      if (!p.isTotalInternalReflection && p.refractedAngleRad !== null && p.refractedAngleDeg! > 1.5) {\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = \'#059669\';\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.8;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.arc(cx, cy, arcR, Math.PI / 2 - p.refractedAngleRad, Math.PI / 2);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n\\n        const midT = Math.PI / 2 - p.refractedAngleRad * 0.45;\\n        const labelR = arcR + 22;\\n        drawHaloText(\\n          ctx,\\n          `\316\270t ${p.refractedAngleDeg!.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n          cx + Math.cos(midT) * labelR + 6,\\n          cy + Math.sin(midT) * labelR + 4,\\n          \'#047857\',\\n          \'600 11.5px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\',\\n          \'left\'\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\",\"StartLine\":296,\"TargetContent\":\"        // Map real penetration depth ratio (delta_e / lambda_0) to crisp pixel decay depth\\n        const ratio =\\n          p.evanescentPenetrationDepthNm !== null\\n            ? clamp(p.evanescentPenetrationDepthNm / wavelengthRef.current, 0.08, 1.8)\\n            : 0.35;\\n        const decayDepthPx = clamp(ratio * 95, 18, height * 0.34);\\n        const kx = (2 * Math.PI * sinI) / lambda1Px;\\n\\n        const spanStart = cx - beamHalfWidth * 0.9;\\n        const spanEnd = Math.min(width - 12, cx + width * 0.42);\\n        const cols = 4;\\n\\n        for (let z = 2; z <= decayDepthPx * 2.6; z += 4) {\\n          const decay = Math.exp(-z / decayDepthPx);\\n          if (decay < 0.04) break;\\n          for (let x = spanStart; x <= spanEnd; x += cols) {\\n            const dx = x - cx;\\n            const envX =\\n              dx < 0\\n                ? Math.exp(-Math.pow(dx / (beamHalfWidth * 0.7), 2))\\n                : Math.exp(-dx / (width * 0.32));\\n            const val = Math.cos(kx * dx - phase) * decay * envX;\\n            if (Math.abs(val) < 0.06) continue;\\n            ctx.fillStyle =\\n              val >= 0\\n                ? hexToRgba(\'#d97706\', Math.abs(val) * 0.65)\\n                : hexToRgba(\'#0f172a\', Math.abs(val) * 0.25);\\n            ctx.fillRect(x, cy + z, cols, 3.2);\\n          }\\n        }\\n\\n        // Draw penetration depth 1/e indicator bracket\\n        const bracketX = Math.min(width - 96, cx + 110);\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = \'#b45309\';\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.4;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.moveTo(bracketX, cy + 2);\\n        ctx.lineTo(bracketX, cy + decayDepthPx);\\n        ctx.moveTo(bracketX - 5, cy + decayDepthPx);\\n        ctx.lineTo(bracketX + 5, cy + decayDepthPx);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n\\n        ctx.font = \'500 11px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\';\\n        ctx.fillStyle = \'#92400e\';\\n        const depthLabel =\\n          p.evanescentPenetrationDepthNm !== null\\n            ? `\316\264e = ${formatWavelength(p.evanescentPenetrationDepthNm)}`\\n            : \'S\303\263ng suy gi\341\272\243m\';\\n        ctx.fillText(depthLabel, bracketX + 8, cy + decayDepthPx * 0.5 + 4);\\n        ctx.restore();\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // 3. Interface Boundary Line & Normal Line\\n    ctx.strokeStyle = \'#334155\';\\n    ctx.lineWidth = 1.75;\\n    ctx.beginPath();\\n    ctx.moveTo(0, cy);\\n    ctx.lineTo(width, cy);\\n    ctx.stroke();\\n\\n    if (ly.angles) {\\n      // Normal line (dashed vertical through origin)\\n      ctx.save();\\n      ctx.strokeStyle = \'#64748b\';\\n      ctx.lineWidth = 1.2;\\n      ctx.setLineDash([5, 5]);\\n      ctx.beginPath();\\n      ctx.moveTo(cx, 16);\\n      ctx.lineTo(cx, height - 16);\\n      ctx.stroke();\\n      ctx.restore();\\n\\n      ctx.font = \'500 11px \\\"Plus Jakarta Sans\\\", sans-serif\';\\n      ctx.fillStyle = \'#64748b\';\\n      ctx.fillText(\'Ph\303\241p tuy\341\272\277n (N)\', cx + 7, 26);\\n\\n      // Optional critical angle reference line in upper-left quadrant\\n      if (p.criticalAngleDeg !== null) {\\n        const cRad = degToRad(p.criticalAngleDeg);\\n        const cLen = maxRayLen * 0.85;\\n        ctx.save();\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = \'rgba(217, 119, 6, 0.55)\';\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.1;\\n        ctx.setLineDash([3, 4]);\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.moveTo(cx, cy);\\n        ctx.lineTo(cx - Math.sin(cRad) * cLen, cy - Math.cos(cRad) * cLen);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n        ctx.restore();\\n\\n        ctx.font = \'500 10.5px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\';\\n        ctx.fillStyle = \'#b45309\';\\n        ctx.fillText(\\n          `\316\270c=${p.criticalAngleDeg.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n          cx - Math.sin(cRad) * (cLen * 0.72) - 46,\\n          cy - Math.cos(cRad) * (cLen * 0.72)\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // 4. E-field oscillation overlays along rays\\n    if (ly.eField) {\\n      drawEFieldVectors(\\n        cx,\\n        cy,\\n        -incDirX,\\n        -incDirY,\\n        maxRayLen * 0.92,\\n        lambda1Px,\\n        0,\\n        1.0,\\n        waveHex,\\n        \'top\',\\n        true\\n      );\\n      if (refAmp > 0.08) {\\n        drawEFieldVectors(\\n          cx,\\n          cy,\\n          refDirX,\\n          refDirY,\\n          maxRayLen * 0.92,\\n          lambda1Px,\\n          refPhaseRad,\\n          refAmp,\\n          \'#dc2626\',\\n          \'top\',\\n          false\\n        );\\n      }\\n      if (!p.isTotalInternalReflection && p.refractedAngleRad !== null && transAmp > 0.08) {\\n        drawEFieldVectors(\\n          cx,\\n          cy,\\n          Math.sin(p.refractedAngleRad),\\n          Math.cos(p.refractedAngleRad),\\n          maxRayLen * 0.92,\\n          lambda2Px,\\n          0,\\n          transAmp,\\n          \'#059669\',\\n          \'bottom\',\\n          false\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // 5. Crisp Ray Arrows (Incident, Reflected, Refracted)\\n    const srcX = cx - incDirX * maxRayLen;\\n    const srcY = cy - incDirY * maxRayLen;\\n\\n    if (ly.rays) {\\n      // Incident ray\\n      drawRayArrow(ctx, srcX, srcY, cx, cy, waveHex, 2.8, 1.0);\\n\\n      // Reflected ray (opacity + thickness scales with sqrt(R))\\n      const refAlpha = clamp(0.18 + refAmp * 0.82, 0.18, 1);\\n      const refWidth = 1.4 + refAmp * 1.8;\\n      drawRayArrow(\\n        ctx,\\n        cx,\\n        cy,\\n        cx + refDirX * maxRayLen,\\n        cy + refDirY * maxRayLen,\\n        \'#dc2626\',\\n        refWidth,\\n        refAlpha\\n      );\\n\\n      // Refracted ray\\n      if (!p.isTotalInternalReflection && p.refractedAngleRad !== null) {\\n        const transAlpha = clamp(0.2 + transAmp * 0.8, 0.2, 1);\\n        const transWidth = 1.4 + transAmp * 1.8;\\n        drawRayArrow(\\n          ctx,\\n          cx,\\n          cy,\\n          cx + Math.sin(p.refractedAngleRad) * maxRayLen,\\n          cy + Math.cos(p.refractedAngleRad) * maxRayLen,\\n          \'#059669\',\\n          transWidth,\\n          transAlpha\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\\n\\n    // 6. Angle Arcs & Numeric Annotations\\n    if (ly.angles) {\\n      const arcR = 52;\\n      // Incident angle arc (measured from top normal -pi/2 counter-clockwise to incident ray)\\n      if (p.incidentAngleDeg > 1.5) {\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = waveHex;\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.arc(cx, cy, arcR, -Math.PI / 2 - thetaI, -Math.PI / 2);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n\\n        const midI = -Math.PI / 2 - thetaI * 0.5;\\n        ctx.font = \'600 11.5px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\';\\n        ctx.fillStyle = \'#0f172a\';\\n        ctx.fillText(\\n          `\316\270i ${p.incidentAngleDeg.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n          cx + Math.cos(midI) * (arcR + 14) - 24,\\n          cy + Math.sin(midI) * (arcR + 14)\\n        );\\n      }\\n\\n      // Reflected angle arc\\n      if (p.incidentAngleDeg > 1.5 && p.reflectanceEffective > 0.002) {\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = \'#dc2626\';\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.4;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.arc(cx, cy, arcR - 10, -Math.PI / 2, -Math.PI / 2 + thetaI);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n\\n        const midR = -Math.PI / 2 + thetaI * 0.5;\\n        ctx.font = \'500 11px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\';\\n        ctx.fillStyle = \'#b91c1c\';\\n        ctx.fillText(\\n          `\316\270r ${p.reflectedAngleDeg.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n          cx + Math.cos(midR) * (arcR + 8) + 2,\\n          cy + Math.sin(midR) * (arcR + 8)\\n        );\\n      }\\n\\n      // Refracted angle arc\\n      if (!p.isTotalInternalReflection && p.refractedAngleRad !== null && p.refractedAngleDeg! > 1.5) {\\n        ctx.strokeStyle = \'#059669\';\\n        ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;\\n        ctx.beginPath();\\n        ctx.arc(cx, cy, arcR, Math.PI / 2 - p.refractedAngleRad, Math.PI / 2);\\n        ctx.stroke();\\n\\n        const midT = Math.PI / 2 - p.refractedAngleRad * 0.5;\\n        ctx.font = \'600 11.5px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\';\\n        ctx.fillStyle = \'#047857\';\\n        ctx.fillText(\\n          `\316\270t ${p.refractedAngleDeg!.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n          cx + Math.cos(midT) * (arcR + 16) + 2,\\n          cy + Math.sin(midT) * (arcR + 16) + 4\\n        );\\n      }\\n    }\",\"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/WaveCanvas.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Refining WaveCanvas angle labels and evanescent wave\",\"toolSummary\":\"Refine WaveCanvas labels & TIR wave\"}"
