  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing New Requirements**\n\nOkay, I\'ve got two new user requests to dive into, and they\'re in Vietnamese. I\'ll need to carefully translate those. Also, I see we need to add the `drawHaloText` helper function to `WaveCanvas.tsx`, per our previous edit, which I\'ll be sure to include when I revise that code.\n\n\n**Implementing PDF Export**\n\nI\'m now focused on the PDF export functionality. I\'ll need to use `jspdf` to generate a report including a header, timestamp, and a live snapshot of the setup. User input parameters and calculated results will also be displayed in the downloadable report, after they are entered directly as numeric inputs and validated.\n\n\n**Adding PDF Diagram**\n\nI\'m now integrating the electromagnetic wave canvas diagram directly into the PDF export, a nice feature! I\'ll include the full suite of input parameters and calculated results, as detailed. Also, I\'ve got a way to ensure proper Vietnamese diacritic rendering within the PDF, even without Unicode hacks \342\200\224 using an offscreen HTML5 Canvas for cleaner, high-DPI typography.\n\n\n**Refining User Interactions**\n\nI\'m now integrating direct drag-and-drop handles onto the canvas, allowing users to intuitively adjust the refractive indices ($n_1$ and $n_2$) of the two media. This builds upon the existing drag-and-drop functionality for changing the incident angle. My goal is to make the interaction as tactile and intuitive as possible. Moreover, I\'m confident about guaranteeing correct Vietnamese character rendering within the PDF reports, and will export a high-resolution A4 page to .pdf. This will ensure a high-quality lab report, and will embed a live ray/wavefront figure!\n\n\n**Enhancing Canvas Interactions**\n\nI\'m now implementing vertical drag handles for refractive indices, complete with draggable knobs and numeric displays. Users can now directly manipulate n1 and n2, in addition to adjusting the incident angle. The refracted ray, deviation angle, wavefront compression, and Fresnel characteristics will all update in real-time. Finally, I\'m adding a visual representation of the ray deviation angle, for intuitive feedback.\n\n\n**Verifying Test Coverage**\n\nOkay, I\'ve confirmed that no new integration skills are needed for `jspdf`. I\'m now making unit test updates for helper functions, then compiling and linting. I\'ll also be restarting the dev server to verify all the critical features. Specifically, I\'ll be testing numeric inputs, drag-and-drop interactions, PDF report generation, and the mobile/desktop layouts. I\'m installing `jspdf` via `install_applet_package`, and simultaneously starting to create the PDF report generator module `src/utils/pdfReport.ts`.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "_MwGa4LpJ6D-z7sP5r7OgQ8"
