  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Report**\n\nI\'m amazed by the generated PDF report, it\'s outstanding! The format presents itself like a published academic optics report. I\'m noting the clean presentation of `n\342\202\202 = 3.5`. This is going to be incredibly useful.\n\n\n**Refining the Output**\n\nI\'ve just updated the diagram and PDF with new values: `\316\270i = 73.30\302\260`, which computed `\316\270t = 15.55\302\260`, `\316\224\316\270 = 57.75\302\260`, `R = 35.8% / T = 64.2%`. There are two small text collisions in `r2-desktop.png` and `r2-mobile.png`. I\'m going to fix them with minor code tweaks: adjusting positions and alignments of text labels within the WaveCanvas.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "g9IGa9vHJt6wmNMPw5qzmQ4"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_10051193562737134032"
      name: "multi_replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"Description\":\"Eliminate \316\270t/\316\224\316\270 label overlap and narrow-canvas mobile HUD label collisions in WaveCanvas.tsx\",\"Instruction\":\"Separate \316\270t and \316\224\316\270 label radii/alignments cleanly and adapt canvas corner HUD labels on narrow viewports (< 520px)\",\"ReplacementChunks\":[{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"EndLine\":498,\"ReplacementContent\":\"      if (width >= 520) {\\n        drawHaloText(\\n          ctx,\\n          \'Ph\303\241p tuy\341\272\277n (N)\',\\n          cx + 8,\\n          24,\\n          \'#64748b\',\\n          \'500 11px \\\"Plus Jakarta Sans\\\", sans-serif\',\\n          \'left\'\\n        );\\n      }\",\"StartLine\":485,\"TargetContent\":\"      drawHaloText(\\n        ctx,\\n        \'Ph\303\241p tuy\341\272\277n (N)\',\\n        cx + 8,\\n        24,\\n        \'#64748b\',\\n        \'500 11px \\\"Plus Jakarta Sans\\\", sans-serif\',\\n        \'left\'\\n      );\"},{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"EndLine\":710,\"ReplacementContent\":\"      // Refracted angle arc & ray deviation (\316\224\316\270) visual cue\\n      if (!p.isTotalInternalReflection && p.refractedAngleRad !== null) {\\n        if (p.refractedAngleDeg! > 1.5) {\\n          ctx.strokeStyle = \'#059669\';\\n          ctx.lineWidth = 1.8;\\n          ctx.beginPath();\\n          ctx.arc(cx, cy, arcR, Math.PI / 2 - p.refractedAngleRad, Math.PI / 2);\\n          ctx.stroke();\\n\\n          // Place \316\270t cleanly below the arc near the normal side so it never collides with \316\224\316\270\\n          const midT = Math.PI / 2 - p.refractedAngleRad * 0.45;\\n          const labelR = arcR + 18;\\n          drawHaloText(\\n            ctx,\\n            `\316\270t ${p.refractedAngleDeg!.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n            cx + Math.cos(midT) * labelR - 4,\\n            cy + Math.sin(midT) * labelR + 12,\\n            \'#047857\',\\n            \'600 11.5px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\',\\n            \'center\'\\n          );\\n        }\\n\\n        // Undeviated dashed ray extension into Medium 2 + deviation angle \316\224\316\270 arc\\n        if (p.deviationAngleDeg !== null && p.deviationAngleDeg > 2.0) {\\n          ctx.save();\\n          ctx.strokeStyle = \'rgba(100, 116, 139, 0.55)\';\\n          ctx.lineWidth = 1.25;\\n          ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);\\n          ctx.beginPath();\\n          ctx.moveTo(cx, cy);\\n          ctx.lineTo(cx + incDirX * maxRayLen * 0.85, cy + incDirY * maxRayLen * 0.85);\\n          ctx.stroke();\\n          ctx.restore();\\n\\n          const devArcR = arcR + 42;\\n          const a1 = Math.PI / 2 - thetaI;\\n          const a2 = Math.PI / 2 - p.refractedAngleRad;\\n          const startA = Math.min(a1, a2);\\n          const endA = Math.max(a1, a2);\\n          ctx.strokeStyle = \'#0284c7\';\\n          ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;\\n          ctx.beginPath();\\n          ctx.arc(cx, cy, devArcR, startA, endA);\\n          ctx.stroke();\\n\\n          const midDev = (startA + endA) * 0.5;\\n          drawHaloText(\\n            ctx,\\n            `\316\224\316\270 ${p.deviationAngleDeg.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n            cx + Math.cos(midDev) * (devArcR + 14) + 6,\\n            cy + Math.sin(midDev) * (devArcR + 14) + 3,\\n            \'#0369a1\',\\n            \'600 10.5px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\',\\n            \'left\'\\n          );\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\",\"StartLine\":653,\"TargetContent\":\"      // Refracted angle arc & ray deviation (\316\224\316\270) visual cue\\n      if (!p.isTotalInternalReflection && p.refractedAngleRad !== null) {\\n        if (p.refractedAngleDeg! > 1.5) {\\n          ctx.strokeStyle = \'#059669\';\\n          ctx.lineWidth = 1.8;\\n          ctx.beginPath();\\n          ctx.arc(cx, cy, arcR, Math.PI / 2 - p.refractedAngleRad, Math.PI / 2);\\n          ctx.stroke();\\n\\n          const midT = Math.PI / 2 - p.refractedAngleRad * 0.45;\\n          const labelR = arcR + 22;\\n          drawHaloText(\\n            ctx,\\n            `\316\270t ${p.refractedAngleDeg!.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n            cx + Math.cos(midT) * labelR + 6,\\n            cy + Math.sin(midT) * labelR + 4,\\n            \'#047857\',\\n            \'600 11.5px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\',\\n            \'left\'\\n          );\\n        }\\n\\n        // Undeviated dashed ray extension into Medium 2 + deviation angle \316\224\316\270 arc\\n        if (p.deviationAngleDeg !== null && p.deviationAngleDeg > 2.0) {\\n          ctx.save();\\n          ctx.strokeStyle = \'rgba(100, 116, 139, 0.55)\';\\n          ctx.lineWidth = 1.25;\\n          ctx.setLineDash([4, 4]);\\n          ctx.beginPath();\\n          ctx.moveTo(cx, cy);\\n          ctx.lineTo(cx + incDirX * maxRayLen * 0.85, cy + incDirY * maxRayLen * 0.85);\\n          ctx.stroke();\\n          ctx.restore();\\n\\n          const devArcR = arcR + 30;\\n          const a1 = Math.PI / 2 - thetaI;\\n          const a2 = Math.PI / 2 - p.refractedAngleRad;\\n          const startA = Math.min(a1, a2);\\n          const endA = Math.max(a1, a2);\\n          ctx.strokeStyle = \'#0284c7\';\\n          ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;\\n          ctx.beginPath();\\n          ctx.arc(cx, cy, devArcR, startA, endA);\\n          ctx.stroke();\\n\\n          const midDev = (startA + endA) * 0.5;\\n          drawHaloText(\\n            ctx,\\n            `\316\224\316\270 ${p.deviationAngleDeg.toFixed(1)}\302\260`,\\n            cx + Math.cos(midDev) * (devArcR + 12) + 4,\\n            cy + Math.sin(midDev) * (devArcR + 12) + 4,\\n            \'#0369a1\',\\n            \'600 10.5px \\\"IBM Plex Mono\\\", monospace\',\\n            \'left\'\\n          );\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\"},{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"EndLine\":780,\"ReplacementContent\":\"    // 8. Medium Labels (Adaptive for desktop vs compact mobile canvas so labels never collide)\\n    const isCompactCanvas = width < 520;\\n    const railX = width - 30;\\n\\n    if (isCompactCanvas) {\\n 