  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Application**: **EMRefract Lab** (`metadata.json` already configured; never rename), a Vietnamese electromagnetic wave refraction simulation and characteristic identification workbench built with React 19, Vite, Tailwind CSS v4, TypeScript, `lucide-react`, `motion` (`motion/react`), and `jspdf`.\n- **Completed Core Scope (earlier turns)**:\n  - Interactive 2D HTML5 Canvas electromagnetic wave refraction simulator (`WaveCanvas.tsx`) with animated wavefronts, rays, E-field polarization vectors, evanescent wave + penetration depth $\\delta_e$ in TIR, ray deviation angle $\\Delta\\theta$, and direct drag-and-drop on canvas for $\\theta_i$, $n_1$, and $n_2$.\n  - Direct numeric inputs + sliders for $\\theta_i$, $n_1$, $n_2$ with inline validation, optical/RF dielectric material catalog, guided scenarios, and high-DPI Vietnamese PDF report export (`exportRefractionPdfReport` via `jspdf`).\n  - Automatic propagation regime classifier & 6-column tabular metrics (`CharacteristicsPanel.tsx`), interactive Fresnel reflectance/phase SVG chart (`FresnelChart.tsx`), inverse wave/material identification lab (`InverseIdentifierView.tsx`), and recorded lab measurement log with CSV export (`MeasurementLogView.tsx`).\n- **Current Follow-Up Requests (just implemented, NOT YET verified/compiled!)**:\n  1. *\"Th\303\252m hi\341\273\207u \341\273\251ng ho\341\272\241t h\341\273\215a m\306\260\341\273\243t m\303\240 (CSS transition ho\341\272\267c framer-motion) cho c\303\241c thanh tr\306\260\341\273\243t trong ControlDeck \304\221\341\273\203 ph\341\272\243n h\341\273\223i tr\341\273\261c quan h\306\241n khi ng\306\260\341\273\235i d\303\271ng thay \304\221\341\273\225i chi\341\272\277t su\341\272\245t ho\341\272\267c g\303\263c t\341\273\233i.\"*\n  2. *\"c\303\263 th\341\273\203 th\303\252m c\303\241c thanh c\303\264ng c\341\273\245 th\341\273\203 hi\341\273\207n tr\341\273\261c quan h\306\241n\"*\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Completed Code Edits (Already Written to Disk \342\200\224 Pending Test, Build, Lint & Browser Verification)\n- **`/src/components/AnimatedLabSlider.tsx`** (created):\n  - Reusable animated slider component using `motion/react` (`motion.div`, `AnimatePresence`, `useReducedMotion`) layered over a native accessible `<input type=\"range\">` (`opacity-0`, full hit area).\n  - Features spring-animated active fill bar (`scaleX`), spring-animated thumb knob with hover/drag/focus tactile halo ring, floating live numeric callout badge on drag/focus (`formatTooltip`), and calibrated physical reference markers (`markers` prop) that smoothly slide along the rail.\n  - Exports `computeSliderPercent(value, min, max)`.\n- **`/src/components/ControlDeck.tsx`** (updated):\n  - Replaced all 4 `<input type=\"range\">` sliders ($\\theta_i$, $n_1$, $n_2$, $\\lambda_0$) with `AnimatedLabSlider`.\n  - Added live calibrated `\316\270B` (amber) and `\316\270c` (rose) reference markers on the incident angle ($\\theta_i$) slider rail.\n  - Added smooth `motion.div` micro-transition on the live `G\303\263c kh\303\272c x\341\272\241 (\316\270t)` and `\304\220\341\273\231 l\341\273\207ch tia (\316\224\316\270)` readout card.\n- **`/src/components/WaveCanvas.tsx`** (updated):\n  - Added **Calibrated Optical Protractor Overlay** (`layers.protractor`, enabled by default) centered on `(cx, cy)` with 5\302\260 minor ticks, 15\302\260/30\302\260 major ticks, and 30\302\260/60\302\260 degree markings.\n  - Upgraded the top toolbar into a clean two-row visual instrument header:\n    - Row 1: Playback (`T\341\272\241m d\341\273\253ng` / `Ph\303\241t s\303\263ng`, `B\306\260\341\273\233c pha`), **Auto Angle Sweep** (`Qu\303\251t g\303\263c` / `D\341\273\253ng qu\303\251t` using `Repeat` icon, sweeps $\\theta_i$ between `5\302\260` and `85\302\260` automatically and stops if user drags canvas), `\304\220\341\272\267t l\341\272\241i`, **Zoom Controls** (`75%`\342\200\223`175%` with `ZoomOut`/`ZoomIn`), and speed selector.\n    - Row 2: Icon-coded layer toggles (`S\303\263ng ph\341\272\263ng`, `Tia s\303\263ng`, `Tr\306\260\341\273\235ng E`, `G\303\263c & \316\224\316\270`, `Th\306\260\341\273\233c \304\221o g\303\263c`) + compact color legend (`Tia t\341\273\233i`, `Ph\341\272\243n x\341\272\241`, `Kh\303\272c x\341\272\241`).\n  - Added a **Live Visual Instrument Strip** directly beneath the canvas stage:\n    - Animated dual-segment **Energy Flux Bar** (`motion.div` spring width split between `Ph\341\272\243n x\341\272\241 R (%)` in rose and `Truy\341\273\201n qua T (%)` in emerald, or `S\303\263ng suy gi\341\272\243m (T = 0%)` in amber during TIR).\n    - Live **Wavelength Compression Gauge** (`\316\273\342\202\201 \342\206\222 \316\273\342\202\202`) with dual inline SVG sine waves visually comparing spatial wavelength in Medium 1 vs Medium 2.\n- **`/src/physics/emPhysics.test.ts`** (updated):\n  - Added test #11 testing `computeSliderPercent` from `../components/AnimatedLabSlider`.\n\n### Skills & References Already Read\n- `ultra-mode` (`/skills/system_skills/ultra_mode/SKILL.md`): active for this conversation. Follow-up changes require **at most 1 targeted verification round** (unit tests + compile + lint + restart dev server + browser check + visual inspection).\n- `computer-use` (`/skills/system_skills/computer_use/SKILL.md`): headless Chromium via `playwright-cli`, always `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`, unique filenames under `.playwright-cli/`, never overwrite earlier screenshot names.\n- `frontend-design` (`/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md`) + `6_education_simulations.md` + `8_science_space_biotech.md`.\n\n### Not Yet Run Since Last Edit\n- Unit tests (`npx --yes tsx --test src/physics/emPhysics.test.ts`) have NOT been run after the latest edits.\n- `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` have NOT been run after the latest edits.\n- `restart_dev_server` has NOT been run after the latest edits.\n- Browser visual verification of the new animated sliders and visual toolbars has NOT been run yet.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Tailwind CSS v4 + Fonts**: `Plus Jakarta Sans` + `IBM Plex Mono` loaded in `index.html` and mapped in `src/index.css`.\n- **Canvas Performance in Headless Chromium**: `WaveCanvas.tsx` throttles 2D `requestAnimationFrame` draws to ~30fps (`now - lastDrawTs >= 32`) and skips redrawing while paused (`!isPlayingRef.current`), with `stepPx = 5` in `drawWavefrontBeam`. This keeps CPU usage low so Playwright screenshots/videos complete reliably without timing out.\n- **PDF Export**: Uses `jspdf` + an offscreen 1240\303\2271754 A4 canvas rendered with browser fonts to preserve full Vietnamese diacritics without garbled glyphs.\n- **Mobile Layout**: Desktop nav sits in `<header>` (`hidden md:flex`), while mobile uses a non-sticky 3-tab strip inside `<main>` (`md:hidden`) and orders `WaveCanvas` above `ControlDeck` (`order-1 lg:order-2`). Compact canvas HUD labels activate at `width < 520` to avoid collisions.\n- **Note on `WaveCanvas.tsx` Row 2 Icon**: Currently `angles` (`G\303\263c & \316\224\316\270`) reuses the `Repeat` icon also used by `Qu\303\251t g\303\263c` in Row 1. During verification/polish (if needed), consider swapping `angles` icon to `SlidersHorizontal` or `TriangleRight` / `DraftingCompass` (or `Ruler`) if `Repeat` looks duplicated visually.\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- **Earlier Round 1 Visual Defects (all fixed)**:\n  - Mobile top bar clipped tabs and stacked `ControlDeck` above canvas \342\206\222 fixed via `hidden md:flex` header nav + non-sticky mobile tab bar + `order-1 lg:order-2`.\n  - Canvas angle labels overlapped rays/wavefronts \342\206\222 fixed via `drawHaloText` + bisector placement + separate radii for `\316\270t` and `\316\224\316\270`.\n  - `M\341\272\253u Ph\341\272\243n x\341\272\241 to\303\240n p...` button truncated \342\206\222 renamed to `G\303\263c Brewster` and `Ph\341\272\243n x\341\272\241 to\303\240n ph\341\272\247n`.\n  - Narrow mobile canvas HUD labels collided \342\206\222 added `isCompactCanvas = width < 520` compact HUD labels.\n- **Playwright Screenshot Timeout (fixed)**:\n  - Continuous 60fps CPU canvas redraw with `strokeText` caused `playwright-cli screenshot` to hit the 20s timeout once.\n  - Fixed by throttling `WaveCanvas` to ~30fps (`>= 32ms`), skipping redraw when paused, and setting `stepPx = 5`. Subsequent screenshots completed cleanly with 0 console errors.\n- **Potential Risk to Watch in Next Step**:\n  - In `src/physics/emPhysics.test.ts`, test #11 imports `../components/AnimatedLabSlider`, which imports `motion/react` and `react`. Verify `npx --yes tsx --test src/physics/emPhysics.test.ts` runs cleanly in Node without DOM/JSX issues; if `motion/react` or `react` causes an issue in Node test runner, move `computeSliderPercent` into a pure utility module (e.g. `src/physics/emPhysics.ts` or `src/utils/sliderMath.ts`) and import it from both `AnimatedLabSlider.tsx` and the test file.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- All files are saved cleanly in `/app/applet`.\n- No background tasks or Chromium sessions are currently running (earlier `playwright-cli` sessions closed via `trap`).\n- Earlier verification screenshots occupy `.playwright-cli/r1-*.png`, `r2-*.png`, `r3-*.png`, `r1-wave-motion.webm`, and a sample PDF. Use fresh unique names like `.playwright-cli/r4-desktop.png`, `.playwright-cli/r4-sliders.webm`, `.playwright-cli/r4-mobile.png`.\n\n## 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Run Unit Tests + Compile + Lint in Parallel**:\n   - `run_command`: `npx --yes tsx --test src/physics/emPhysics.test.ts` (if `AnimatedLabSlider` import fails under Node due to `motion/react`, extract `computeSliderPercent` into `src/physics/emPhysics.ts` or a pure helper and re-run).\n   - `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` in the same turn.\n2. **Restart Dev Server**:\n   - Call `restart_dev_server` so headless Chromium loads the newly compiled bundle (`DISABLE_HMR=true`).\n3. **Run Targeted Follow-Up Browser Verification (1 round max per Ultra Mode)**:\n   - Use `playwright-cli` with `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT` at `1440x900` (and quick check at `390x844`):\n     - Capture `.playwright-cli/r4-desktop.png` inspecting:\n       - New animated sliders in `ControlDeck` (including `\316\270B` / `\316\270c` calibrated markers on the `\316\270i` slider).\n       - New two-row visual canvas toolbar (playback, `Qu\303\251t g\303\263c`, Zoom `100%`, icon-coded layer toggles, color legend).\n       - Optical protractor overlay on the canvas.\n       - Live animated Energy Flux Bar (`Ph\341\272\243n x\341\272\241 R` / `Truy\341\273\201n qua T`) and Wavelength Compression SVG gauge beneath the canvas.\n     - Record a short `.webm` video (`.playwright-cli/r4-sliders.webm`) interacting with:\n       - Clicking `G\303\263c Brewster` and `Ph\341\272\243n x\341\272\241 to\303\240n ph\341\272\247n` to verify spring animation on sliders and energy flux bar.\n       - Dragging/changing the `\316\270i` or `n\342\202\202` slider to see floating live value callout badge & spring animation.\n       - Toggling `Qu\303\251t g\303\263c`, `ZoomIn` (`125%`), and `Th\306\260\341\273\233c \304\221o g\303\263c` on/off.\n     - Capture `.playwright-cli/r4-mobile.png` at `390x844` to verify the new two-row toolbar and energy/wavelength strip reflow cleanly with zero horizontal overflow.\n     - Check `playwright-cli console` (must have 0 errors/warnings).\n4. **Inspect All Captures & Fix Any High/Medium Defects**:\n   - Visually inspect `r4-desktop.png`, `r4-mobile.png`, and `r4-sliders.webm`.\n   - Note: Check if the `angles` toggle button icon (`Repeat` duplicated with `Qu\303\251t g\303\263c`) or protractor labels overlap any ray labels; if anything needs a surgical fix, apply it, then re-run unit tests + `compile_applet` + `lint_applet` + `restart_dev_server` + quick screenshot check before finishing (never finish on a stale check).\n5. **Final Response**:\n   - Respond in concise, plain-language Vietnamese (2\342\200\2233 sentences max), confirming the smooth spring slider animations (`motion/react`) with floating value callouts and `\316\270B`/`\316\270c` markers, plus the upgraded visual instrument toolbars (optical protractor, zoom, auto angle sweep, icon-coded layers, and live energy flux & wavelength comparison bar).\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Language**: 100% Vietnamese UI copy and Vietnamese final response matching the user\'s language.\n- **Communication Style**: Keep the final response to 2\342\200\2233 simple, plain-language sentences max; omit code snippets, file paths, routine passing check logs, and hype.\n- **Design Constitution**: Zero static pill badges on metadata, zero `//` mechanical prefixes, zero decorative pulsing dots, zero thick `border-l-4` accents, strict 3-zone top bar, `prefers-reduced-motion` compliance, single-line buttons (`whitespace-nowrap shrink-0`).\n- **Verification Discipline**: Never claim anything was verified without running it after the last code edit; co-execute `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` on the final build check; always trap `playwright-cli close` on exit.\n</summary>"
