    thinking: "**Initiating Browser Verification**\n\nOkay, I\'ve started the targeted browser verification round. I\'ve opened `http://localhost:3000` at `1440x900`, snapped a desktop screenshot, and started inspecting the snapshot and console logs. Next, I\'ll check the mobile view.\n\n\n**Refining Playwright Integration**\n\nI\'m now streamlining the verification process. Instead of separate steps, I\'m focusing on a single, clean shell script utilizing `trap` for error handling and `playwright-cli run-code`. This session will open the page, capture desktop snapshots and console logs, and record an interactive `.webm` video. Inside this session, I\'ll leverage accessible role locators within `playwright-cli run-code` to smoothly click specific elements, and control video recordings with appropriate pauses. This should give cleaner results.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Snapshotting Accuracy**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing snapshot verification. I plan to resize to `390x844`, check for horizontal overflow, and capture a `.playwright-cli/r4-mobile.png` screenshot along with console output. I realize checking the accessibility tree via snapshot is much faster than inspecting code. I\'ll focus on getting this step done first before moving onto the quick recording.\n\n\n"
