  planner_response {
    response: "\304\220\303\243 ho\303\240n t\341\272\245t n\303\242ng c\341\272\245p hi\341\273\207u \341\273\251ng ho\341\272\241t h\341\273\215a l\303\262 xo m\306\260\341\273\243t m\303\240 cho to\303\240n b\341\273\231 thanh tr\306\260\341\273\243t trong b\341\272\243ng \304\221i\341\273\201u khi\341\273\203n (`G\303\263c t\341\273\233i \316\270i`, `Chi\341\272\277t su\341\272\245t n\342\202\201`, `Chi\341\272\277t su\341\272\245t n\342\202\202`, `B\306\260\341\273\233c s\303\263ng \316\273\342\202\200`) k\303\250m th\341\272\273 gi\303\241 tr\341\273\213 n\341\273\225i theo th\341\273\235i gian th\341\273\261c khi k\303\251o v\303\240 v\341\272\241ch \304\221\303\241nh d\341\272\245u t\341\273\261 \304\221\341\273\231ng t\341\272\241i g\303\263c Brewster (`\316\270B`) v\303\240 g\303\263c t\341\273\233i h\341\272\241n (`\316\270c`).\n\nKhu v\341\273\261c s\303\242n kh\341\272\245u m\303\264 ph\341\273\217ng c\305\251ng \304\221\306\260\341\273\243c b\341\273\225 sung c\303\241c thanh c\303\264ng c\341\273\245 tr\341\273\261c quan h\306\241n, bao g\341\273\223m ch\341\272\277 \304\221\341\273\231 qu\303\251t g\303\263c t\341\273\261 \304\221\341\273\231ng (`Qu\303\251t g\303\263c`), thu ph\303\263ng s\306\241 \304\221\341\273\223 (`75%\342\200\223175%`), th\306\260\341\273\233c \304\221o g\303\263c quang h\341\273\215c tr\303\252n n\341\273\201n canvas, c\303\241c n\303\272t b\341\272\255t/t\341\272\257t l\341\273\233p hi\341\273\203n th\341\273\213 c\303\263 bi\341\273\203u t\306\260\341\273\243ng tr\341\273\261c quan, c\303\271ng thanh \304\221o ph\303\242n b\341\273\225 n\304\203ng l\306\260\341\273\243ng (`R / T`) v\303\240 \304\221\341\273\223 th\341\273\213 n\303\251n\342\200\223gi\303\243n b\306\260\341\273\233c s\303\263ng (`\316\273\342\202\201 \342\206\222 \316\273\342\202\202`) c\341\272\255p nh\341\272\255t theo th\341\273\235i gian th\341\273\261c."
    thinking: "**Inspecting The Captures**\n\nI\'m diving deep into the provided captures! Specifically, I\'m carefully analyzing `r5-desktop.png`. Its aesthetic strikes me as clean and balanced, with a distinctly scientific instrument vibe. I\'m keen to dissect every visual element thoroughly to understand its implications!\n\n\n**Analyzing Visual Flow**\n\nI\'m now focused on the video `r5-sliders.webm`. The initial frames, specifically 00:00-00:13, reveal the slider animations. The tooltip badges for `\316\270i` are clean and intuitive. The `Ph\341\272\243n x\341\272\241 to\303\240n ph\341\272\247n` activation and the Energy Flux Bar\'s smooth transitions catch my attention. It\'s really interesting how the amber and rose markers behave!\n\n\n**Observing Smooth Transitions**\n\nI\'m presently zeroing in on the observed animations within `r5-sliders.webm`. I\'m especially fascinated by how, when the rose reflection reaches 100%, and the wave comparison turns amber, the evanescent wave moves along the boundary with no jitter. Smooth scaling happens when I magnify the wave diagram. Also, the incident angle sweeps and updates in real time, with the other components smoothly updating as well, at the same time.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "ZuQGa7aCC76AkdUP-t-BuQc"
