  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Database Schema**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased to report that I\'ve just completed a comprehensive verification. Every single table and column within `information_schema.columns` perfectly aligns with the specifications detailed in `src/db/schema.ts`! This confirmation includes the precise matching of tables like `users` and `measurements`, along with their respective columns. This is a huge step!\n\n\n**Integrating New Schema Fields**\n\nI\'m now deeply immersed in integrating the newly verified schema fields into the application. Specifically, I\'m focusing on wiring up those fields, like `material2_id`, `incident_angle_deg`, etc., into `src/main.tsx`, `src/App.tsx`, and `src/components/MeasurementLogView.tsx`. Furthermore, I\'m designing and executing unit tests for `src/physics/emPhysics.test.ts`. Currently, I\'m concentrating on `MeasurementLogView` and incorporating a clean sign-in/sign-out bar, minimizing any SQL or database jargon.\n\n\n**Refining App Layout**\n\nI\'m currently revising the `src/App.tsx` layout. I\'m focusing on the tab structure, specifically the `\'LAB_3D\'` view, ensuring that the `<WaveScene3D />` component is rendered full-bleed for optimal 3D scene display. I\'m also ensuring the `<header>` remains a three-zone display. Additionally, I\'m integrating the Cloud SQL measurement persistence. Upon user sign-in, I\'ll fetch and display saved measurement records.\n\n\n**Implementing Measurement Persistence**\n\nI\'m now implementing measurement persistence. Upon user sign-in, I fetch and display saved measurement records. If the user is a guest, I\'ll store the measurements locally in state. I\'m focusing on seamless integration, and I\'ll prompt guests gently via a status banner if they may like to sign-in, without any SQL jargon. I\'m also ensuring clean deletion, with calls to `DELETE /api/measurements/:id` or `DELETE /api/measurements` when deleting persisted records. When the user selects \"\303\201p d\341\273\245ng n\342\202\202 = ...\", I\'ll be updating `n2` and `material2Id` and switching smoothly to `SIMULATOR`, with a clear banner.\n\n\n\n"
