  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 1
    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Application**: **EMRefract Lab** (`metadata.json` already configured; never rename), a Vietnamese electromagnetic wave refraction simulation and characteristic identification workbench built with React 19, Vite, Tailwind CSS v4, TypeScript, Express, Drizzle ORM + Cloud SQL (PostgreSQL), Firebase Auth (Google Sign-In), Three.js, `motion`, `lucide-react`, `jspdf`, and `@google/genai`.\n- **Completed Earlier Scope**:\n  - 2D interactive HTML5 Canvas electromagnetic wave refraction simulator (`WaveCanvas.tsx`), smooth spring-animated sliders (`AnimatedLabSlider.tsx`, `ControlDeck.tsx`), automatic propagation regime classifier (`CharacteristicsPanel.tsx`), interactive Fresnel SVG chart (`FresnelChart.tsx`), inverse wave/material identifier (`InverseIdentifierView.tsx`), PDF report export (`pdfReport.ts`), and lab measurement log (`MeasurementLogView.tsx`).\n- **Current User Request**: *\"h\303\243y th\303\252m nh\341\273\257ng ti\341\273\207n \303\255ch n\303\240y\"* with 3 explicit features attached:\n  1. **Three.js 3D scenes** (`threejs` skill): Full-bleed interactive 3D optical refraction bench with composite 3\342\200\22312 part PBR models, `RoomEnvironment`, `ACESFilmicToneMapping`, warm/cool lighting + horizon fog, software-WebGL `afterDraw()` pacing, animated 3D E-field waves, `InstancedMesh` photonic wavefronts, damped `OrbitControls`, camera presets, and collapsible bottom control dock.\n  2. **Add a SQL database (Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL)** (`cloudsql-setup` + `cloudsql-update-schema` + `cloudsql-execute-sql` skills): Provisioned Cloud SQL PostgreSQL instance (`ai-studio-ab69d8c7` in `asia-southeast1`, project `proven-impact-rdrm3`), configured Firebase Auth Google Sign-In (`set_up_oauth`), built Drizzle ORM schema & repository, pushed & verified schema, and integrated seamless authenticated persistence for measurements and search logs (with strict UI isolation \342\200\224 zero SQL/DB status exposed in UI).\n  3. **Use Google Search data** (`gemini-api` skill): Server-side `gemini-4-hydrogen` + `{ googleSearch: {} }` endpoint (`POST /api/search/material`) powering the `Tra c\341\273\251u v\341\272\255t li\341\273\207u` tab (`MaterialSearchView.tsx`) with verified clickable web source citations, refractive index extraction (`[N_INDEX: ...]`), one-click apply to simulator, and synced history for signed-in users.\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Provisioning & Infrastructure (100% Complete & Verified)\n- **Cloud SQL Eligibility & Provisioning**:\n  - `cloudsql.CheckFeatureEligibility` -> eligible (`proven-impact-rdrm3`).\n  - User confirmed via `show_aistudio_ui` (`\"Enable Cloud SQL in region asia-southeast1\"`).\n  - `cloudsql.CreateInstance` (`region: \"asia-southeast1\"`) -> created `ai-studio-ab69d8c7`.\n  - `set_up_oauth` (`scopes_to_add: [\"openid\", \"email\", \"profile\"]`, `userConfirmedInUI: true`) -> generated `/firebase-applet-config.json` (`projectId: \"proven-impact-rdrm3\"`).\n  - Packages installed in one batched call: `firebase`, `firebase-admin`, `drizzle-orm`, `drizzle-kit`, `pg`, `@types/pg`, `three`, `@types/three`, `@google/genai@latest`.\n  - `cloudsql.UpdateSchema` -> created `users`, `measurements`, `search_logs` with FKs.\n  - `cloudsql.ExecuteSql` (`SELECT ... FROM information_schema.columns ...`) -> confirmed all 3 tables and every column exist in `public` schema matching `/src/db/schema.ts`.\n\n### Code Files Created & Updated (All Saved, Compiled, Linted & Unit-Tested)\n- **`/package.json`**: Updated scripts to `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"` and `\"start\": \"node server.ts\"`.\n- **`/src/db/schema.ts`**: Drizzle PostgreSQL tables (`users`, `measurements`, `searchLogs`) + `relations`.\n- **`/src/db/drizzle.config.ts`**: Admin Drizzle Kit config (`SQL_HOST`, `SQL_DB_NAME`, `SQL_ADMIN_USER`, `SQL_ADMIN_PASSWORD`, `ssl: false`).\n- **`/src/db/index.ts`**: Object Method `pg.Pool` cached on `global._postgresPool` using `SQL_*` env vars, no startup probes or reconnect loops.\n- **`/src/db/repository.ts`**: Parameterized Drizzle queries with two-layer error translation (`getOrCreateUser` upsert, `listUserMeasurements`, `createUserMeasurement`, `deleteUserMeasurement`, `clearUserMeasurements`, `listUserSearchLogs`, `saveUserSearchLog`), all strictly scoped by authenticated user.\n- **`/src/lib/firebase.ts`** & **`/src/lib/firebase-admin.ts`**: Client & Admin Firebase Auth using static JSON import of `../../firebase-applet-config.json`.\n- **`/src/middleware/auth.ts`**: `requireAuth` & `optionalAuth` Express middleware verifying `Authorization: Bearer <token>` via `adminAuth.verifyIdToken` and syncing user to PostgreSQL.\n- **`/src/utils/searchUtils.ts`**: Pure helpers (`sanitizeGroundedSources` restricting links to `http:`/`https:`, `extractRefractiveIndexFromText`, `stripInternalIndexTag`).\n- **`/src/lib/gemini.ts`**: Server-side `@google/genai` client (`User-Agent: \'aistudio-build\'`) calling `gemini-4-hydrogen` with `tools: [{ googleSearch: {} }]`.\n- **`/server.ts`**: Full-stack Express server on port 3000 with input validation, authenticated `/api/measurements` CRUD, `/api/search/material` (clean `429`/`403`/`502` Vietnamese error translation), `/api/search/history`, and `vite.middlewares` in dev / `dist/` in prod.\n- **`/src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx`** & **`/src/main.tsx`**: Google `signInWithPopup` AuthProvider with in-memory `getIdToken()`.\n- **`/src/three/opticalBenchGeometry.ts`**: Pure 3D beam vector math (`computeOpticalBenchVectors3D`) + procedural `CanvasTexture` maps (anodized M6 breadboard + bump, 360\302\260 calibrated goniometer dial, soft radial contact shadow) + 4 composite 3\342\200\22312 part PBR `THREE.Group` models (Optical Bench + 4 LatheGeometry isolation legs + Brass Bezel, 8-part Articulated Laser Emitter, 6-part Semicircular Dielectric Prism + Titanium Cradle + Medium 1 Aura, 5-part Photodetector Receiver Arm).\n- **`/src/components/WaveScene3D.tsx`**: Full-bleed Three.js 3D lab with `RoomEnvironment` + `PMREMGenerator`, `ACESFilmicToneMapping`, warm key + cool `HemisphereLight` + rim light + matching `Fog`, `isSoftwareGl` guard with `afterDraw()` fenceSync pacing, dynamic 3D E-field wave ribbons (TE/TM/Unpolarized + evanescent TIR wave), `InstancedMesh` photon wavefronts, damped `OrbitControls` & camera presets (`T\341\273\225ng quan`, `T\341\273\253 tr\303\252n xu\341\273\221ng`, `M\341\272\267t ph\303\242n c\303\241ch`, `C\341\272\255n c\341\272\243nh tr\306\260\341\273\235ng E`), and collapsible bottom dock (`H` shortcut, zero `backdrop-filter` over WebGL).\n- **`/src/components/MaterialSearchView.tsx`**: Google Search Grounding UI (`Tra c\341\273\251u v\341\272\255t li\341\273\207u`) with preset optical/RF queries, verified web citations, one-click `\303\201p d\341\273\245ng n\342\202\202` into simulator, and synced history for signed-in users.\n- **`/src/components/MeasurementLogView.tsx`** & **`/src/App.tsx`**: Added 5-tab navigation (`M\303\264 ph\341\273\217ng 2D`, `Ph\303\262ng lab 3D`, `Nh\341\272\255n d\341\272\241ng ng\306\260\341\273\243c`, `Tra c\341\273\251u v\341\272\255t li\341\273\207u`, `B\341\272\243ng ph\303\251p \304\221o`), full-bleed 3D layout, Google Sign-In/Sign-Out controls, and seamless PostgreSQL sync.\n- **`/src/physics/emPhysics.test.ts`**: Expanded to 13 unit tests (all 13 passing).\n\n### Verification Status Before Compaction\n- **Unit tests** (`npx --yes tsx --test src/physics/emPhysics.test.ts`): **13/13 PASS**.\n- **`compile_applet` & `lint_applet`**: Both **PASSED** with 0 errors.\n- **API Auth check**: `GET /api/measurements` without token returned **`401`** as expected.\n- **Browser captures inspected**:\n  - `.playwright-cli/r6-3d-motion.webm`: Verified 3D TIR transition (laser swings to 55\302\260, beam turns 633nm red, reflects 100% into photodetector, amber evanescent surface wave hugs interface, camera smoothly transitions to top-down and back).\n  - `.playwright-cli/r7-3d-lab.png` (1440\303\227900): **Looks great!** Entire 3D optical bench, brass goniometer, laser emitter, dielectric glass prism, photodetector, 3D E-field ribbons, and photon nodes frame cleanly above the bottom dock.\n  - `.playwright-cli/r7-search.png` (1440\303\227900): Clean UI displaying our formatted Vietnamese `429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` notice pointing to `Settings > Secrets` (no raw JSON, no fake fallback).\n  - `.playwright-cli/r7-log.png` (1440\303\227900): Clean Measurement Log with `\304\220\304\203ng nh\341\272\255p Google \304\221\341\273\203 l\306\260u l\303\242u d\303\240i`, zero SQL/DB jargon exposed.\n  - `.playwright-cli/r7-3d-mobile.png` (390\303\227844): **CAUGHT 1 REAL MOBILE LAYOUT DEFECT** (see Errors & Fixes + Next Steps below!).\n\n### Skills Read (Already Applied)\n- `cloudsql-setup`, `cloudsql-update-schema`, `cloudsql-execute-sql`, `threejs` (+ `fundamentals.md`, `lighting.md`, `materials.md`, `interaction.md`), `gemini-api` (+ `tools_and_grounding.md`), `ultra-mode` (+ `games_3d.md`), `computer-use`, `securecoder-persona`.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Gemini API Quota in Current Container**: Calling `POST /api/search/material` hits `gemini-4-hydrogen` with `{ googleSearch: {} }` properly on the server, and the container\'s `GEMINI_API_KEY` currently returns `429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` (\"You exceeded your current quota, please check your plan and billing details\"). Per `gemini-api` skill rules, NEVER mask this with fake/hardcoded search responses; our server cleanly returns HTTP `429` with a helpful Vietnamese message advising the user to check quota or select a billing-enabled key in **Settings > Secrets**, and we must mention this honestly in the final response.\n- **Dependency Audit (`bun audit`)**: Ran read-only `bun audit`; only transitive advisories in `@grpc/grpc-js` (unused Firestore compat inside `firebase`/`firebase-admin`) and dev-only `esbuild` (`drizzle-kit`/`tsx`/`vite`).\n- **3D Scene Camera Framing**: `ISO: [-6.0, 6.4, 8.8] -> [0, 1.35, 0.45]` frames the bench cleanly on desktop above the bottom dock.\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n1. **TS2339 in `WaveScene3D.tsx`**: Initially referenced `p.phaseShiftReflectedPDeg` / `p.phaseShiftReflectedSDeg` instead of `p.phaseShiftPDeg` / `p.phaseShiftSDeg` from `WavePhysicsResult`. **Fixed** and verified with `tsc --noEmit`.\n2. **Raw JSON 502 on Gemini 429 in `server.ts`**: Initial `POST /api/search/material` returned `502` with raw stringified JSON on Gemini quota errors. **Fixed** by translating `429`/`RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` -> HTTP `429` and `403`/`API_KEY_INVALID` -> HTTP `403` with clean Vietnamese guidance pointing to `Settings > Secrets`.\n3. **UNRESOLVED MOBILE DEFECT (Just spotted in `.playwright-cli/r7-3d-mobile.png` at 390\303\227844)**:\n   - In `/src/components/WaveScene3D.tsx` inside the collapsible bottom dock (`role=\"group\" aria-label=\"G\303\263c nh\303\254n camera 3D\"`), the camera preset container uses `inline-flex items-center gap-1 pl-1.5 border-l border-slate-200` **WITHOUT `flex-wrap`**!\n   - As a result, on narrow mobile (`390px`), the 4th button `\"C\341\272\255n c\341\272\243nh tr\306\260\341\273\235ng E\"` overflows and gets clipped at the right edge of the white dock card (`C\341\272\255n c\341\272\243nh tr...`), AND the dock itself is quite tall on 390px when expanded (covering the bottom ~40% of the mobile 3D viewport, clipping the bottom slider slightly).\n   - **Concrete Fix**:\n     - Add `flex-wrap` and remove `border-l pl-1.5` on small screens (`sm:pl-1.5 sm:border-l sm:border-slate-200`) on the camera preset `role=\"group\"`, and shorten `\"C\341\272\255n c\341\272\243nh tr\306\260\341\273\235ng E\"` to `\"Tr\306\260\341\273\235ng E\"` (or `\"C\341\272\255n c\341\272\243nh\"`) so all 4 buttons fit cleanly inside the dock on 390px with zero clipping.\n     - On mobile (`< 640px`), make the bottom dock slightly more compact (`p-2.5 sm:p-3.5 space-y-2 sm:space-y-3`, `max-h-[46vh] overflow-y-auto`, and default `dockExpanded` to collapsed on narrow mobile OR compact 3-column sliders / tighter spacing) so none of the 3 sliders clip at the bottom of the 844px mobile viewport!\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Express + Vite dev server is running cleanly on port 3000.\n- No background tasks or Playwright Chromium sessions are open (`trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT` closed cleanly).\n- Cloud SQL PostgreSQL instance `ai-studio-ab69d8c7` has verified `users`, `measurements`, and `search_logs` tables.\n- Only the 1 targeted mobile dock layout fix in `/src/components/WaveScene3D.tsx` remains before final verification and response.\n\n## 6. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Fix Mobile Bottom Dock Clipping in `/src/components/WaveScene3D.tsx`**:\n   - Update the camera preset `role=\"group\"` to `flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1 sm:pl-1.5 sm:border-l sm:border-slate-200` (and label `\'C\341\272\255n c\341\272\243nh\'` instead of `\'C\341\272\255n c\341\272\243nh tr\306\260\341\273\235ng E\'`).\n   - Tighten mobile dock padding/spacing (`bottom-3`, `p-2.5 sm:p-3.5`, `space-y-2 sm:space-y-3`, `max-h-[50vh] overflow-y-auto`, `grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-2 sm:gap-3`) so on `390x844` ALL buttons and ALL 3 sliders (`\316\270i`, `n\342\202\201`, `n\342\202\202`) are 100% visible with zero right-edge or bottom-edge clipping.\n2. **Run Final Verification After Last Edit**:\n   - Co-execute `compile_applet`, `lint_applet`, and `npx --yes tsx --test src/physics/emPhysics.test.ts` in parallel.\n   - Call `restart_dev_server`.\n   - Run 1 quick targeted Playwright mobile screenshot check (`.playwright-cli/r8-3d-mobile.png` at `390x844` on `Ph\303\262ng lab 3D`, plus overflow check & `playwright-cli console`, with `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`) to confirm the mobile dock clipping is 100% fixed!\n3. **Final User Response (Vietnamese, concise)**:\n   - Follow `communication_style` + `ultra-mode` + `securecoder-persona` Tier 2 Step 3:\n     - Confirm all 3 features are live in plain Vietnamese (Three.js 3D optical bench in `Ph\303\262ng lab 3D`, Cloud SQL PostgreSQL persistence via Google Sign-In in `B\341\272\243ng ph\303\251p \304\221o`, and Google Search data lookup powered by `gemini-4-hydrogen` in `Tra c\341\273\251u v\341\272\255t li\341\273\207u`).\n     - Include 2\342\200\2233 brief plain-language security safeguards (per `securecoder-persona` Tier 2 Step 3: API keys stay on the server, database queries are parameterized, and saved-data routes verify Google sign-in).\n     - Honestly note the 1 observed runtime constraint: when testing live Google Search lookup in the current environment, Gemini API returned a quota limit (`429 RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED`), so the user may need to check quota or select a billing-enabled API key in **Settings > Secrets** for live search responses.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Language**: 100% Vietnamese UI copy and Vietnamese final response.\n- **Cloud SQL UI Isolation**: NEVER mention Cloud SQL/PostgreSQL status, connection logs, or SQL queries inside the web UI.\n- **No Fake Fallbacks**: Never fake Google Search responses when Gemini returns `429`.\n- **Verification Discipline**: Always run `compile_applet`, `lint_applet`, unit tests, `restart_dev_server`, and inspect the new mobile screenshot AFTER editing `WaveScene3D.tsx` \342\200\224 never finish on a stale check.\n- **Concise Chat Output**: Keep the final response crisp, friendly, and free of code snippets, file paths, or internal jargon (`SecureCoder`, `CWE`, step IDs).\n</summary>"
