  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing an AI Predictor**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing an AI system to predict wave propagation direction. I\'m exploring the use of server-side Gemini (`gemini-4-hydrogen`) with a structured JSON `responseSchema` to ensure scientifically rigorous and visually integrated results. The goal is a deeply useful application.\n\n\n**Defining Feature Sets**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing architectural design and feature specifications for the AI-powered wave propagation predictor. I\'m focusing on defining two seamless modes within a dedicated panel in the EMRefract Lab: analyzing current simulation configurations and enabling custom scenario input. My aim is to create a truly integrated scientific instrument feature, not a generic chatbot add-on, making it a natural extension of the simulator.\n\n\n**Refining Scenario Inputs**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the \"Natural Language Scenario\" input mode. I\'m focusing on user input, specifically scenarios described in Vietnamese. The Gemini `gemini-4-hydrogen` server calls will use a strict `responseSchema` with parameters like `scenarioSummary`, inferred optical parameters (`inferredN1`, etc.), and `directionCategory` for straightforward integration into simulations. My goal is to extract relevant physics from Vietnamese natural language, and prepare it for simulation.\n\n\n**Validating Output Structure**\n\nI\'m now deeply involved in validating the structured output from the AI, specifically the `responseSchema`. I\'m focusing on ensuring accuracy with parameters like `directionCategory` (`AWAY_FROM_NORMAL`, etc.) and the detailed Vietnamese labels. My aim is to make sure the physical reasoning, and engineering recommendations are scientifically sound and actionable. I\'m also ensuring the predicted angles and confidence levels are correctly returned.\n\n\n**Integrating Physics Results**\n\nI\'m now focused on the integration of physics results. I\'ve built a utility module to cross-check the AI\'s predictions against Snell/Fresnel equations and render an interactive SVG. This diagram will display the AI-predicted trajectory, angles, and direction. There will also be buttons for direct simulation input, a physics cross-check strip to show delta errors, and strict error handling to ensure transparency.\n\n\n**Verifying API Usage**\n\nI\'m now methodically verifying the usage of the Gemini API. I\342\200\231ve ensured clean Vietnamese error messages point to **Settings > Secrets** for quota or key issues. I\'ve double-checked the `gemini-4-hydrogen` model doesn\'t require the paid flow, which I confirmed by cross-referencing lines 64-118 in `gemini-api/SKILL.md`. I\'m strictly avoiding deprecated parameters, employing the `@google/genai` `Type` enum, and using the `response.text` property. I am also making sure the code is strictly server-side.\n\n\n**Adding AI Feature**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating the new \"D\341\273\261 \304\221o\303\241n AI\" tab into the application\'s navigation, ensuring a clean and intuitive user experience across devices. I\'m focusing on the best layout, considering both desktop and mobile views. The desktop design remains clean, while the mobile layout will use a horizontally scrollable pill strip for easy access to all tabs. I\'m also adding a direct button link within the 2D Simulator to seamlessly pre-fill the AI prediction with the current simulation state.\n\n\n**Testing AI Functionality**\n\nI\'m now writing thorough unit tests for the `/src/utils/aiWavePrediction.ts` helper module, and adding these tests into `/src/physics/emPhysics.test.ts`. I am creating tests to validate the Gemini JSON response, and also cross-checking the AI prediction against Snell/Fresnel equations to render SVG trajectories. I am focusing on various scenarios including normal refraction, total internal reflection, and grazing/normal incidence. I\'m also preparing for tests that reject invalid payloads, and will calculate Snell discrepancies. I will begin by verifying the \"D\341\273\261 \304\221o\303\241n AI\" tab, testing both preset scenarios and current-state sync toggles.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "rRoHa7eIO4PBvdIPpPO52Qg"
