  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing User Feedback**\n\nI\'m digging into that recent user comment about the app\'s fonts. I\'m focusing on the specific wording and reasoning provided. My goal is to extract the core needs, and consider implications for the next iteration of the app.\n\n\n**Addressing Font Issues**\n\nI\'ve uncovered the root cause of the font issues, and I\'m quite concerned about it. The app loads fonts without proper Vietnamese optimization, and the type scale is incredibly cramped. Everything is using tiny font sizes, especially in Vietnamese, where diacritics need more space. Headings are barely larger than body text, leading to a flat hierarchy and poor readability. The WaveCanvas is particularly bad, using monospace, which causes more trouble with stacking accents.\n\n\n**Refining Typeface Choices**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on specific font pairings. I\'m leaning toward Be Vietnam Pro for display/headings, given its Vietnamese diacritic mastery. I\'m considering Manrope for body text and UI, which is also a solid option. IBM Plex Sans has also been suggested, and is particularly strong for technical content. I\'m focusing on the font\'s weight and optical balance.\n\n\n**Defining Font Specifications**\n\nI\'m solidifying the font specifications for an optimal user experience. I\'ve chosen **`Be Vietnam Pro`**, **`IBM Plex Sans`**, and **`JetBrains Mono`**, for display, technical body and UI, and data/formulas respectively. All Vietnamese diacritics render perfectly. I\'m carefully constructing the type scale, eliminating eye-straining sizes for a balanced visual hierarchy.\n\n\n**Establishing Type Scale Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the specifics of the type scale. I\'m increasing the readability of body text to 14\342\200\22315px and upgrading the font sizes for form elements and UI. I\'ve also set larger, mono-spaced fonts for telemetry readouts. I\'m focusing on consistency, with 12px being the minimum acceptable size for micro-captions. I\'m also ensuring the wave canvas\' fonts use the new choices.\n\n\n"
