    thinking: "**Analyzing Visual Data**\n\nI\'m incredibly excited! Just reviewed the insights from inspecting `.playwright-cli/r9-2d-typography.png` and `.playwright-cli/r9-3d-mobile.png`. The visual inspection was immensely beneficial. The screenshots are proving to be quite valuable and offer some exciting results.\n\n\n**Discovering Font Pairing Improvements**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the new font pairing! The visual improvements are stark, especially with Vietnamese diacritics and tabular numerals. The screenshots `.playwright-cli/r9-2d-typography.png` and `.playwright-cli/r9-3d-mobile.png` clearly show this. I\'ve been diving into a real bug from `.playwright-cli/r9-3d-mobile.png` regarding a desktop header showing on a mobile screen size, where the CSS scaling was misbehaving.\n\n\n**Investigating Hidden Elements**\n\nI\'m deep in it now! Just found an issue in `src/App.tsx`. The `lg:hidden` on the mobile nav is causing unexpected behavior at 390x844. I\'m puzzled, since the `h-15` seems normal. It appears the screenshot was taken *after* a viewport resize.  I need to figure out why the mobile nav was hidden, when its supposed to be visible at that size. It seems like the media query is firing at the incorrect viewport size.\n\n\n**Unraveling Viewport Issues**\n\nI\'m now fixated on the unexpected desktop layout in the 390px screenshot. The `@media` query\'s activation is a mystery! The `EMRefract Lab` and `M\303\264 ph\341\273\217ng` positions in `r9-3d-mobile.png` point to this problem. I need to figure out why Playwright rendered the desktop stylesheet, even after the viewport was set to a mobile size. I will be inspecting `document.documentElement.scrollWidth` and `window.innerWidth`. I will look at `AiWavePredictorView.tsx` to get to the bottom of this perplexing issue.\n\n\n**Uncovering Width Discrepancies**\n\nI\'ve hit another snag! The layout in `r9-3d-mobile.png` is still perplexing. The text overflows, and a button exceeds the 390px width. I\'m focusing on `AiWavePredictorView.tsx` and the `hidden lg:flex` in `src/App.tsx`. I noticed `EMRefract Lab` and `M\303\264 ph\341\273\217ng` are at the same x-coordinates in both the 2D and 3D screenshots! This confirms the issue is a 1440px layout viewport, but I can\'t explain why. I\'ll need to figure out why this happened, when the initial viewport meta tag is defined correctly, and worked in prior screenshots.\n\n\n"
