  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing the Chart**\n\nI\'m focusing on the `RefractiveIndexComparisonChart.tsx` component and its logic in `src/utils/refractiveComparison.ts`. The goal is to make it visually appealing, scientifically sound, and extraordinarily useful. I\'m prioritizing decoupled logic for clarity and maintainability.\n\n\n**Integrating the Simulator**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated the refractive index comparison chart directly below the `FresnelChart` within the 2D Simulator workspace of **EMRefract Lab**. I\'m focusing on the logic within `/src/utils/refractiveComparison.ts`, specifically the `buildRefractiveComparisonData` function. This includes refining the material sorting and category filtering to ensure accurate and comprehensive data representation. The `maxScale` calculation has been updated to prevent clipping. I\'m prioritizing logical soundness.\n\n\n**Enhancing User Interactivity**\n\nI\'m now implementing interactive features for the refractive index chart. My focus is on making the data instantly accessible, so I\'m working to display *n\342\202\202* across all rows to provide immediate context for *n\342\202\201* and *n\342\202\202* values relative to known materials. Calculations for the nearest library material and optical contrast are also in progress. I want to create interactive one-click material assignment via a toggle. I\'m prioritizing user experience.\n\n\n**Crafting the Visuals**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual presentation of the refractive index comparison chart, aiming for a clean and informative design that complements the existing components. Specifically, I\'m working to integrate a `Bi\341\273\203u \304\221\341\273\223 so s\303\241nh chi\341\272\277t su\341\272\245t (n\342\202\201, n\342\202\202) v\341\273\233i th\306\260 vi\341\273\207n v\341\272\255t li\341\273\207u` title, a concise unboxed summary with precise optical contrast data, and interactive controls, including a category filter and quick-assign toggle for interactive material selection. I am prioritizing a visually appealing and intuitive layout.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Refraction**\n\nI\'m now focused on the chart\'s visual elements, aiming for clarity and precision. I\'m working with vertical reference lines for *n\342\202\201* and *n\342\202\202*, using Sky and Indigo colors with collision avoidance for their tags. I\'m adding a shaded optical contrast span to visually represent the refractive jump, and each material row will be a semantic button with name, tags, and animated bar. I want this to be intuitive.\n\n\n**Refining the Chart**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the interactive elements and data representation within the refractive index chart. Specifically, I\'m working on animating `motion.div` spring width bars, distinctly coloring them based on their active states (n\342\202\201, n\342\202\202, both, or library baseline). I\'m also ensuring right-aligned, tabular-nums for *n* and *\316\265r* values using JetBrains Mono. In addition, I\'m creating a concise insight strip at the bottom, dynamically displaying surrounding library materials for custom *n\342\202\201*/*n\342\202\202* values. The goal is to provide a clear and intuitive user experience with immediate insights. I\'m focusing on the component\'s interactive logic to ensure seamless data updates as the user interacts with the chart.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "BqsHa7KIK-fzvdIP4MKzeQ"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_13537349819433055873"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import { clamp } from \'../physics/emPhysics.ts\';\\nimport { OPTICAL_MATERIALS, OpticalMaterial } from \'../physics/materials.ts\';\\n\\nexport type ComparisonCategoryFilter = \'ALL\' | \'GAS_LIQUID\' | \'OPTICAL\' | \'RF_SEMI\';\\n\\nexport interface ComparisonBarItem {\\n  material: OpticalMaterial;\\n  widthPct: number;\\n  isCurrentN1: boolean;\\n  isCurrentN2: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface MaterialBracketSummary {\\n  exactMatch: OpticalMaterial | null;\\n  nearest: OpticalMaterial;\\n  lowerNeighbor: OpticalMaterial | null;\\n  upperNeighbor: OpticalMaterial | null;\\n  deltaToNearest: number;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface RefractiveComparisonModel {\\n  minScale: number;\\n  maxScale: number;\\n  ticks: number[];\\n  items: ComparisonBarItem[];\\n  n1Pct: number;\\n  n2Pct: number;\\n  spanLeftPct: number;\\n  spanWidthPct: number;\\n  ratioN2ToN1: number;\\n  deltaN: number;\\n  n1Bracket: MaterialBracketSummary;\\n  n2Bracket: MaterialBracketSummary;\\n  markersAreClose: boolean;\\n}\\n\\nconst MATCH_EPSILON = 0.004;\\n\\nexport function filterMaterialsByGroup(\\n  materials: OpticalMaterial[],\\n  filter: ComparisonCategoryFilter\\n): OpticalMaterial[] {\\n  if (filter === \'ALL\') return materials;\\n  if (filter === \'GAS_LIQUID\') {\\n    return materials.filter(\\n      (m) => m.category === \'Kh\303\255 & Ch\303\242n kh\303\264ng\' || m.category === \'Ch\341\272\245t l\341\273\217ng\'\\n    );\\n  }\\n  if (filter === \'OPTICAL\') {\\n    return materials.filter((m) => m.category === \'Th\341\273\247y tinh & Quang h\341\273\215c\');\\n  }\\n  return materials.filter((m) => m.category === \'B\303\241n d\341\272\253n & RF\');\\n}\\n\\nexport function findMaterialBracket(\\n  n: number,\\n  sortedMaterials: OpticalMaterial[]\\n): MaterialBracketSummary {\\n  let nearest = sortedMaterials[0];\\n  let bestDelta = Math.abs(sortedMaterials[0].refractiveIndex - n);\\n  let exactMatch: OpticalMaterial | null = null;\\n  let lowerNeighbor: OpticalMaterial | null = null;\\n  let upperNeighbor: OpticalMaterial | null = null;\\n\\n  for (const mat of sortedMaterials) {\\n    const delta = Math.abs(mat.refractiveIndex - n);\\n    if (delta < bestDelta) {\\n      bestDelta = delta;\\n      nearest = mat;\\n    }\\n    if (delta <= MATCH_EPSILON && (!exactMatch || delta < Math.abs(exactMatch.refractiveIndex - n))) {\\n      exactMatch = mat;\\n    }\\n    if (mat.refractiveIndex < n - MATCH_EPSILON) {\\n      lowerNeighbor = mat;\\n    } else if (mat.refractiveIndex > n + MATCH_EPSILON && upperNeighbor === null) {\\n      upperNeighbor = mat;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  return {\\n    exactMatch,\\n    nearest,\\n    lowerNeighbor,\\n    upperNeighbor,\\n    deltaToNearest: bestDelta,\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function normalizeRefractiveIndexToPct(\\n  n: number,\\n  minScale: number,\\n  maxScale: number\\n): number {\\n  if (maxScale <= minScale) return 0;\\n  return clamp(((n - minScale) / (maxScale - minScale)) * 100, 0, 100);\\n}\\n\\nexport function buildRefractiveComparisonModel(params: {\\n  n1: number;\\n  n2: number;\\n  material1Id: string;\\n  material2Id: string;\\n  categoryFilter?: ComparisonCategoryFilter;\\n}): RefractiveComparisonModel {\\n  const { n1, n2, material1Id, material2Id, categoryFilter = \'ALL\' } = params;\\n\\n  // Deduplicate vacuum vs air in the visual bar list? Keep all library entries sorted ascending\\n  // except skip \'vacuum\' only if \'air\' is present and vacuum isn\'t explicitly selected, so the bar\\n  // chart doesn\'t show two nearly identical 1.000 bars stacked on top of each other.\\n  const allSorted = [...OPTICAL_MATERIALS].sort((a, b) => a.refractiveIndex - b.refractiveIndex);\\n  const displayPool = allSorted.filter(\\n    (m) => m.id !== \'vacuum\' || material1Id === \'vacuum\' || material2Id === \'vacuum\'\\n  );\\n\\n  const filtered = filterMaterialsByGroup(displayPool, categoryFilter);\\n\\n  const minScale = 1.0;\\n  const maxVal = Math.max(3.5, n1, n2);\\n  const maxScale = maxVal <= 3.5 ? 3.5 : Math.ceil(maxVal * 10) / 10 + 0.1;\\n\\n  const ticks: number[] = [];\\n  for (let t = 1.0; t <= maxScale + 1e-6; t += 0.5) {\\n    ticks.push(Math.round(t * 10) / 10);\\n  }\\n\\n  const n1Pct = normalizeRefractiveIndexToPct(n1, minScale, maxScale);\\n  const n2Pct = normalizeRefractiveIndexToPct(n2, minScale, maxScale);\\n\\n  const items: ComparisonBarItem[] = filtered.map((material) => {\\n    const isCurrentN1 =\\n      (material1Id === material.id && Math.abs(material.refractiveIndex - n1) < 0.01) ||\\n      Math.abs(material.refractiveIndex - n1) <= MATCH_EPSILON;\\n    const isCurrentN2 =\\n      (material2Id === material.id && Math.abs(material.refractiveIndex - n2) < 0.01) ||\\n      Math.abs(material.refractiveIndex - n2) <= MATCH_EPSILON;\\n\\n    return {\\n      material,\\n      widthPct: normalizeRefractiveIndexToPct(material.refractiveIndex, minScale, maxScale),\\n      isCurrentN1,\\n      isCurrentN2,\\n    };\\n  });\\n\\n  const n1Bracket = findMaterialBracket(n1, allSorted);\\n  const n2Bracket = findMaterialBracket(n2, allSorted);\\n\\n  return {\\n    minScale,\\n    maxScale,\\n    ticks,\\n    items,\\n    n1Pct,\\n    n2Pct,\\n    spanLeftPct: Math.min(n1Pct, n2Pct),\\n    spanWidthPct: Math.abs(n2Pct - n1Pct),\\n    ratioN2ToN1: n2 / Math.max(1e-6, n1),\\n    deltaN: n2 - n1,\\n    n1Bracket,\\n    n2Bracket,\\n    markersAreClose: Math.abs(n2Pct - n1Pct) < 13,\\n  };\\n}\\n\",\"Description\":\"Create pure comparison chart data model, normalization, and nearest-material bracket calculator\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/utils/refractiveComparison.ts\",\"toolAction\":\"Creating refractive comparison logic\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create refractiveComparison.ts utility\"}"
      thinking_signature: "\022\377:\n\374:\001i\024}\023\233\340\020\335\317A\230\0069#\241\225\323\260\356\377\021\320N~O\320\a=\214\0014\035u\237\336\026N\262(~\302\366\263\177\362\241\227l\0036\352g\312\340\363\251\376\206]\230\334\310y[$<\343\226\272\000u\336~G\305\202\266\270\362R\2474=5\023\001\027\204\2113\2569\323\232^B\274L\316\253G\335\036\177\247A\000\204i\340\035d\202hW\"\347\374\2425r\034\027Q\225\030\261W\024d\371\242\va&J\205\251\354\033\252\305h\361\313\2776w~T\343\220\262\261,\325\344\234\255\234_\337\347H\202&~~w\304d\321\323\002b\246\362k)5\371tQ\271\257*\336\243:\001\310\2270\364\207\327*PD\332\232\364x\355\325:\217\341\343P\355\374\r\032\312\362\r\356\326\252<t;\206\026\177<>9\222\336(\236\373\025\272iF,A\264\242\236}\212\207\367NZ\266\232\035\253\247W\232W\r\223\232\212\203\304\265^\242\271\214\237\340\200(#\361\315M\217\264\366\214E\302\251\243\333\340\021\304\237\332_\234\312\322e\v\343H\016J\365\v)7\006\217\027\346\352\244U*_\233\354\204\342\022\337\207\360\265\331\222\272d\201\377\2337s\350BFU\206\211\324\233\317C\266\"\332H\005\367\374\vX\032\345OH\262\335\016\017Zf6u\351T\006@\215<{\343H\230ec\222=q$\350\311b\241\367\365\333~\337D\210\365{\274\031\031w3\t\004\f\260x_3\003&\230\344{\242\305w\200\221\fi\f-&\312\362\263\177\310\340T0o\214\372\267\327\302:D\204y),\302\235\223\243\335\022\227\024L\337\216~\307S\212\364\330\3726\245\371\002\246\016|\210=]\333z\313ql\001\346\300\201\322\to\034\306\362o\243\3601\323p\025[\273\264\251X\326\265X\363\232E\361\200\177\335\324e\377`1\030\362\253L\200\217\026\fb\036x:\357\005\324\234{\tsP!\245,\352\\\367\257\205\367\363\302(\2412\275x\005e\"\t\340\314j\vj\203c\003\277S\366\256fZr\313\253{\332-Q\356!-Q\343\223\nQ><+\202\216z\366_\"s\316\2466\306\311\306\037\302Xq1\360%\362o\365\274\373u\262\247\020R7wSw\264\314\273\030P\022\257\aH\371Df\325\3007^ \300\220\207bq\230\330Z\021\034\366\377\315\367Jk/\350\245u\303\021P\315\262v\362\344\240\364\317]\352?\364\031h\243mV\245c\330\347\235f\3271G\353\255\211Z~\0