  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Inspecting Implementation**\n\nOkay, I\'m examining `RefractiveIndexComparisonChart.tsx` now. Lines 177-200 are the current focus. Specifically, I\'m noting the `n1` marker label and its style attribute, especially the `transform: \'translateX(-` component. I\'m trying to determine the impact of this particular style declaration before making any code edits. I\'ll need to examine the other marker styles as well, to confirm the appropriate scope of our adjustments.\n\n\n**Analyzing Transformations**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down on those `translateX` style declarations. It looks like at the extreme ends of the spectrum, the labels are overflowing their bounds. My solution is a helper function to conditionally apply the `translateX` value based on the percentage marker position, so as not to overflow the column widths. I\'m also confirming the column width calculations on mobile devices, to ensure everything fits properly, and considering the available widths within padding.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile Layout**\n\nI\'m now focused on optimizing the chart\'s mobile layout. The existing calculations were yielding a very cramped middle track on small screens. I\'ve recalculated the grid columns and increased the available width considerably. I\'m also considering hiding intermediate axis ticks on smaller devices to prevent label overlap and ensure readability. My next step will be to test this thoroughly and address any remaining edge cases.\n\n\n"
