  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Pixel Alignment**\n\nI\'m struck by the pixel-perfect alignment observed in the desktop comparison image. Specifically, the value `n\342\202\202 = 2.050` is positioned exactly where it should be. The clarity of this alignment is quite impressive, really solidifying our assessment of the render.\n\n\n**Analyzing Mobile Display**\n\nI\'m now focused on the mobile display and observing the axis ticks. I\'ve noted the alignment of the `3.0` tick at 80% and the `3.5` tick at the edge. The alignment here offers new insights into scaling across devices, which helps solidifiy our work! I\'m paying close attention to this.\n\n\n**Refining Mobile Tick Display**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the overlapping tick labels on the mobile display. I realize that the proximity of ticks like \'3.0\' and \'3.5\' is the core issue. I\'ve developed a concise solution: filter the labels for small screens. My one-line fix, `showOnMobile = isFirst || isLast || (idx % 2 === 0 && pct <= 72)`, offers clear spacing with any maximum scale. It offers so much clarity now!\n\n\n"
    message_id: "TrQHa53aDYikvdIPtfPKyAU"
