  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Tooltip UX**\n\nI\'m focusing now on the user experience design for the scientific material index tooltip. I\'m prioritizing clarity and informative depth for each tooltip, specifically for the `RefractiveIndexComparisonChart`. I\'m starting to visualize a clean and intuitive layout that emphasizes key data.\n\n\n**Computing Tooltip Data**\n\nI\'ve been working on a new helper function, `buildMaterialIndexTooltipData`, designed to compute precise electromagnetic and optical properties directly from a material\'s refractive index. This function now calculates various properties, including relative permittivity, phase velocity, wavelength scale percentage, impedance, and the critical angle for total internal reflection when exiting into air. The function is designed with unit tests for reliability.\n\n\n**Expanding Material Understanding**\n\nI\'m now integrating richer explanations of refractive index values. I\'ve calculated the Brewster angle from air and included the Abbe number for chromatic dispersion, with Vietnamese interpretations. I\'m also computing the immediate delta of the refractive index against current simulation values. Furthermore, I\'m working on adding detailed two-sentence Vietnamese explanations for each material\'s refractive index to explain why it has that value. I\'m considering adding an optional `indexExplanation` directly to the `OpticalMaterial` definition for a single source of truth.\n\n\n**Validating Index Explanation**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that adding an optional or required `indexExplanation: string` field to `OpticalMaterial` won\'t break any existing functionality. I double-checked the usage of `OPTICAL_MATERIALS` across `findMaterialById`, `identifier.ts`, `ControlDeck.tsx`, and `RefractiveIndexComparisonChart.tsx`, and it looks like a clean, maintainable solution.\n\n\n**Positioning Tooltips Strategically**\n\nI\'m now focusing on tooltip positioning to prevent viewport clipping and unwanted flicker. I\'m currently working to develop smart anchoring logic, considering the row\'s position within the chart. My plan is to use `event.currentTarget.offsetTop` and `offsetHeight` to dynamically position tooltips above or below rows, using a crisp pointer arrow for clarity. I\'m trying to ensure the tooltips are always visible without obscuring other chart elements.\n\n\n**Refining Tooltip Placement**\n\nI\'m now refining the tooltip placement logic for improved visibility and user experience. I\'ve realized `event.currentTarget.getBoundingClientRect()` offers better control, especially for vertical positioning. I\'m implementing a check to determine if the tooltip should be placed above or below the row based on available space. Horizontally, I\'m working to make the placement centered on the bar track to avoid overflow. This ensures the tooltip is always fully visible, regardless of screen size.\n\n\n**Optimizing Tooltip Positioning**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing desktop and mobile tooltip positioning. For desktop, I\'m centering the 380px tooltip card around the bar midpoint, clamping within the plot width. On mobile, I\'m ensuring the tooltip spans full width, positioned above or below the row. For robust positioning, I\'m placing the tooltips inside a `relative` plot wrapper, using `top` or `bottom` and horizontal positioning with `left-0 right-0 sm:left-[210px] sm:right-auto sm:w-[400px]`, and clamping to avoid overflow.\n\n\n**Designing Tooltip Style**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the visual design of the floating tooltip. I\'m focusing on creating a light scientific instrument card that visually matches the \"EMRefract Lab\" theme. This includes a white background with a subtle backdrop blur, a rounded border, and a shadow. I\'m using `motion.div` for a subtle fade-in animation, which is instantly disabled when `prefersReducedMotion`. The header will contain the material name, category, and the refractive index value. I\'m planning to include a concise explanation of `n` in Vietnamese as well.\n\n\n**Constructing Tooltip Metrics**\n\nI\'m now implementing a 2x2 tabular grid to present key optical and electromagnetic properties for each material in the tooltip. This includes phase velocity, relative permittivity, wavelength compression, and critical/Brewster angles. The data is calculated from the refractive index (`n`), with corresponding Vietnamese interpretations. I\'ll also add a footer line for live comparisons against the current simulation values.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Tooltip Affordance**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing consistent visibility and affordance. I\'m keeping the comparison bracket summary always visible to prevent jumping. I\'ve added a tiny info icon next to the material name, and I\'m updating the helper text. This ensures the user can view both tooltip and summary at once, improving UX. I\'m also adding accessibility features, like the `aria-describedby` attribute to link tooltips.\n\n\n**Implementing Tooltip Interactivity**\n\nI\'m now implementing interactive features for the tooltip, including an active row button with the `id=\"material-index-tooltip\"` and `role=\"tooltip\"`. I\'m supporting the `Escape` key for dismissing the tooltip when it has keyboard focus. I\'ll need to edit `/src/physics/materials.ts`, `/src/utils/refractiveComparison.ts`, and `/src/components/RefractiveIndexComparisonChart.tsx` in parallel, and add unit tests to `/src/physics/emPhysics.test.ts`.\n\n\n"
